WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你制作了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们两人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.560
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:32.510
Today, we are slipping into your feed early this week because after this, we are going to go on a vacay.
今天，我们提前在本周出现在你的订阅列表中，因为在这之后，我们要去度假了。

9
00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:33.910
Vacation.
度假。

10
00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.190
My birthday's coming up.
我的生日快到了。

11
00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.030
It's summer.
现在是夏天。

12
00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.050
We're going to go spend some time with our families.
我们要去陪陪家人。

13
00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:38.930
That's right.
没错。

14
00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:43.790
We'll be back on July 13th with Secretary's Day with special guest Ellie Kemper.
我们将在7月13日回归，带来《秘书日》那一集，并有特邀嘉宾艾丽·坎伯尔。

15
00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:45.410
Oh, it's so fun.
噢，那集太有趣了。

16
00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:49.190
But today, we're going to talk to you all about Happy Hour.
但今天，我们要和大家聊聊《欢乐时光》那一集。

17
00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:53.150
It is Season 6, Episode 21, written by B.J.
这是第六季第21集，由B.J.诺瓦克编剧，

18
00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:55.250
Novak, directed by Matt Sohn.
马特·索恩执导。

19
00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:56.990
Would you like a summary?
你想听听剧情摘要吗？

20
00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.170
Boy, would I.
天哪，我太想听了。

21
00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:05.010
Oscar organizes a happy hour for everyone in The Office as an excuse to spend time with Matt from The Warehouse.
奥斯卡组织了一场办公室欢乐时光，借口是为了和仓库的马特多待一会儿。

22
00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:11.330
Pam invites a friend to the bar as a kind of setup for Michael because what is she thinking?
帕姆邀请了一位朋友去酒吧，想给迈克尔做媒，她到底在想什么？

23
00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:12.770
Pam, Pam, Pam, Pam.
帕姆，帕姆，帕姆，帕姆。

24
00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:17.090
But the setup is foiled by Michael's alter ego, Date Mike.
但这场相亲被迈克尔的另一个自我“约会迈克”给搅黄了。

25
00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:24.890
Meanwhile, Andy and Aaron are trying to keep their dating life a secret to avoid any drama that might come from openly dating a fellow co-worker.
与此同时，安迪和艾琳试图对他们的恋情保密，以避免公开与同事约会可能带来的任何麻烦。

26
00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:30.290
But in the end, Andy has a pretty fantastic grand announcement.
但最终，安迪做了一个相当精彩的隆重宣布。

27
00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:31.050
He does.
他确实做了。

28
00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:36.370
And one thing to add to your summary, Angela's going to debut some bright red lipstick.
还要给你的摘要补充一点，安吉拉要首次涂上鲜红色的口红。

29
00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:41.910
I noticed that, and I was hoping you were going to talk about it.
我注意到了，我正希望你会谈谈这个。

30
00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:42.750
Oh, I will.
噢，我会的。

31
00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:49.090
Fast fact number one, this episode was directed by our camera operator, Matt Sohn.
第一个速记事实，这一集是由我们的摄影师马特·索恩执导的。

32
00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:53.070
This was the first episode of The Office that he directed.
这是他执导的第一集《办公室》。

33
00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:54.570
He's directed many more.
后来他又执导了很多集。

34
00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.730
We've talked about him a lot.
我们经常提到他。

35
00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:59.430
Yes, because he's an amazing, awesome person.
是的，因为他是一个了不起、很棒的人。

36
00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:01.790
We were so excited for him to direct.
我们当时非常兴奋能让他执导。

37
00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:09.250
Yeah, well, he said we were very supportive, but he also said we gave him a little s*** throughout the week.
是啊，他说我们非常支持他，但也说我们在那一周里没少给他找麻烦。

38
00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:11.690
Well, it's because we had all become such close friends.
嗯，那是因为我们已经成了非常亲密的朋友。

39
00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:12.290
It's true.
确实。

40
00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:13.530
So we messed with him a little bit.
所以我们稍微捉弄了他一下。

41
00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:15.670
But it was like the way you tease someone you love.
但这就像是你调侃自己爱的人那样。

42
00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:17.830
Well, as you can tell, I reached out to Matt.
嗯，如你所见，我联系了马特。

43
00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:25.210
He shared some of his memories of directing, but he also gave us some s*** because we've not had him on the podcaSt.
他分享了一些执导时的回忆，但也吐槽了我们，因为我们一直没请他上播客。

44
00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:27.010
Oh, he threw us some shade.
噢，他确实损了我们几句。

45
00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:32.830
I want to point out, my memory is that Rain gave him the most s*** on set.
我想指出的是，我的记忆中，雷恩在片场给他找的麻烦最多。

46
00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:33.150
Yeah.
没错。

47
00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:34.590
You might be right.
你说得可能没错。

48
00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:35.050
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

49
00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:36.270
I mean, that tracks.
我是说，这很符合他的风格。

50
00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:36.610
Right.
对吧。

51
00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:43.230
I told Matt I was kind of shocked that he hasn't been on the podcast because I feel like we talk about him all the time.
我跟马特说，他没上过我们的播客让我挺惊讶的，因为我觉得我们老是在聊他。

52
00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:48.610
I mean, he's the one who gets all of the background glances and everything.
我是说，他可是那个总是被人在背后指指点点的人。

53
00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:51.530
He's the reason half of accounting stuff makes it in.
会计部有一半的东西能成，全靠他。

54
00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:53.330
Well, here's what Matt had to say.
好吧，马特是这么说的。

55
00:02:53.510 --> 00:03:01.450
He said that Randall Einhorn was the cinematographer for this episode, and that made everything a lot easier.
他说兰德尔·艾因霍恩是这一集的摄影指导，这让一切都变得容易多了。

56
00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:01.890
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

57
00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:05.110
Because he and Randall both operated the cameras for years.
因为他和兰德尔两人操作摄像机很多年了。

58
00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:07.090
They had worked together a long, long time.
他们在一起共事了很长很长的时间。

59
00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:12.130
He said he had the advantage of knowing the material very well, knowing the world very well.
他说他有优势，因为他非常了解剧本素材，也非常了解这个世界。

60
00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:16.350
He felt like he had everyone's trust, so he didn't have to do a lot of catch-up or make any introductions.
他觉得大家都信任他，所以他不需要花太多时间去补课或做自我介绍。

61
00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:22.510
And then he also sent in this audio clip about what it meant to him to get to direct this episode.
然后他还发来一段音频，讲了能执导这一集对他意味着什么。

62
00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:34.170
I was a camera operator on the show since season one and was very fortunate that Greg Daniels gave me the opportunity to direct my first episode of television.
我从第一季开始就是这部剧的摄像师，非常幸运的是，格雷格·丹尼尔斯给了我执导人生中第一集电视剧的机会。

63
00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:42.250
You know, Randall Einhorn, Dave Rogers, Dean Holland, Claire Scanlon were all crew members who also got this opportunity,
你知道，兰德尔·艾因霍恩、戴夫·罗杰斯、迪恩·霍兰德、克莱尔·斯坎伦，这些剧组成员也都得到了这个机会，

64
00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:47.130
and all of us are full-time directors today because of Greg Daniels.
而我们现在全都是全职导演，这都要归功于格雷格·丹尼尔斯。

65
00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:54.170
His kindness and generosity to let us get these opportunities, you know, led to my career plus many other careers.
他那种让我们获得这些机会的善良和慷慨，你知道，成就了我的职业生涯，也成就了许多其他人的职业生涯。

66
00:03:54.810 --> 00:04:03.530
Well, that is so true, and we've talked about that many times, about how Greg was such a great creative collaborator and opened the doors for so many people.
嗯，这话说得太对了，我们聊过很多次了，格雷格是一位多么出色的创意合作伙伴，他为多少人打开了大门。

67
00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:04.210
Yeah.
没错。

68
00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:06.510
All right, are you ready for fastback number two?
好了，准备好进行第二个快问快答了吗？

69
00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:07.510
I guess so.
我想好了。

70
00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:08.030
All right.
好。

71
00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:09.370
We're moving on really quickly.
我们节奏很快啊。

72
00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:12.410
Well, I have a fan question from Charlie B.
好吧，我有一个来自华盛顿州塔科马市查理·B的粉丝提问。

73
00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:13.550
in Tacoma, Washington.
在西德和德克斯特酒吧的场景，也就是我们去喝欢乐时光的地方，真的是在戴夫与巴斯特餐厅拍的吗？

74
00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:22.110
Were the scenes at Sid and Dexter's, which is where we go for happy hour, actually filmed at a Dave and Buster's?
答案是，算是吧。

75
00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.870
The answer is, sort of.
那是一家以前的戴夫与巴斯特餐厅，现在叫吉利安餐厅。

76
00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:30.410
It was a former Dave and Buster's that is now called Jillian's.
它位于环球影城步行街。

77
00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:33.130
It was at Universal CityWalk.
大家知道环球影城步行街是什么吗？

78
00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:35.370
Do people know what Universal CityWalk is?
嗯，你知道，我们有环球影城，他们确实有摄影棚，人们经常在那里拍摄各种电视节目和电影。

79
00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:43.590
Well, you know, we have Universal Studios, and they actually have soundstages where people are filming regularly different TV shows, movies.
但在摄影棚后面，山顶上还有一个完整的主题公园。

80
00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:50.810
But then in the back of the studio, you have a whole theme park, like up on this hilltop above it.
那里有各种游乐设施，应有尽有。

81
00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.990
And there's all the rides and, like, everything.
嗯。

82
00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:55.010
Yeah.
然后环球影城步行街就像是一个巨大的户外购物中心，里面全是商店和一家电影院。

83
00:04:55.230 --> 00:05:02.570
And then the Universal CityWalk is kind of like this big outdoor mall that's filled with shops and a movie theater.
没错。

84
00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:03.010
Yeah.
还有吉利安餐厅。

85
00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.190
And Jillian's.
在吉利安餐厅里面，有各种游戏，所有的街机游戏和台球桌。

86
00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:09.890
Inside Jillian's, they had all those games, all the arcade games and pool tables.
但有两款游戏是我们必须自带的，因为剧本里明确提到了，而现场实际上并没有。

87
00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:16.770
But there were two games that we had to bring in because they were specified in the script and they were not actually at the location.
哪两款？

88
00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:17.750
Which ones?
等等，等等，等等。

89
00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:18.330
Wait, wait, wait.
让我猜猜。

90
00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:18.870
I'm going to guess.
让我猜猜。

91
00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:19.390
I'm going to guess.
那个跳舞机。

92
00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:20.710
The dance thing.
没错。

93
00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:21.390
Yes.
好的。

94
00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:21.850
Okay.
那个投篮机？

95
00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:23.690
The basketball hoop thing?
不对，那个本来就在那儿。

96
00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:24.650
Nope, that was there.
啊。

97
00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:25.150
Ah.
嗯。

98
00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:26.470
Hmm.
它在一个你参与的情节里非常显眼，安吉拉。

99
00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:30.590
It figures prominently in a plot that you are involved in, Angela.
哦，打地鼠游戏。

100
00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.150
Oh, Whack-A-Mole.
没错。

101
00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:32.890
Whack-A-Mole.
打地鼠。

102
00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:34.350
That's right.
没错。

103
00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:37.550
That was info thanks to Randy Cordray.
多亏了兰迪·科德雷提供的信息。

104
00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:45.930
And then I also asked Matt about shooting at this location because I was like, Matt, you finally get to direct an episode and it's not at Dunder Mifflin.
我还问了马特关于在这个外景地拍摄的事，因为我当时想，马特，你终于有机会执导一集了，结果却不在邓德·米夫林公司拍。

105
00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:49.710
The majority of it happens at this location that we've never gone to ever.
大部分戏份都发生在这个我们从未去过的地方。

106
00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:52.270
And you know the wheels come off whenever we go on location.
你知道的，只要我们一出外景，准会出乱子。

107
00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:53.530
Oh, we don't travel well.
噢，我们不擅长外景拍摄。

108
00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:56.930
Here is what Matt had to say about shooting on location.
以下是马特关于外景拍摄的看法。

109
00:05:56.930 --> 00:06:04.670
You know, one of the biggest challenges for this episode was that it was almost entirely shot on location.
你知道，这一集最大的挑战之一就是它几乎完全是在外景地拍摄的。

110
00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:10.990
Charles McDougall, another one of the directors from the office, gave me a great piece of advice.
查尔斯·麦克杜格尔，办公室的另一位导演，给了我一个很棒的建议。

111
00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:19.730
He told me to go to the location and to just sit and watch to understand where people hang out, you know,
他让我去外景地坐着观察，去了解人们平时都在哪里消磨时间，你知道的，

112
00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:26.070
where the waiters and waitresses travel and how people naturally work and play in that environment.
服务员们怎么走动，人们在那种环境下是如何自然地工作和娱乐的。

113
00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:34.970
So the weekend before we started shooting, I spent several hours at the Dave and Buster's at Universal CityWalk where we were shooting the episode.
所以，在开拍前的那个周末，我在环球影城步行街的戴夫与巴斯特餐厅待了几个小时，也就是我们拍摄这一集的地方。

114
00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:45.530
And, you know, I just sat and watched so I understood how to make the place feel as natural and real as possible when we were shooting the episode there.
你知道，我只是坐在那里观察，这样我就能明白在拍摄时如何让那个地方看起来尽可能自然和真实。

115
00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:50.830
I thought it was super helpful and worked really great in the episode.
我觉得这非常有帮助，在这一集里的效果也很棒。

116
00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:52.890
So that's amazing advice.
这真是个绝妙的建议。

117
00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:53.510
So smart.
太聪明了。

118
00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:54.090
Incredible.
不可思议。

119
00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:55.810
Way to go, Charles McDougall.
干得好，查尔斯·麦克杜格尔。

120
00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:56.650
Yeah.
是啊。

121
00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:57.390
Action!
开始！

122
00:06:57.890 --> 00:06:58.490
Action!
开始！

123
00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:00.890
I want to point out one thing.
我想指出一件事。

124
00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:01.390
Yeah.
嗯。

125
00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:03.310
There is a DVD commentary for this episode.
这一集有DVD评论音轨。

126
00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:08.230
It has Matt Stone, Brian, Oscar, BJ, and myself.
参与的有马特·斯通、布莱恩、奥斯卡、BJ和我自己。

127
00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:18.110
And Matt talked about shooting at Universal Studios and that it was unique for us because we had never shot anything there on the actual Universal property,
马特谈到了在环球影城拍摄的事，他说这对我们来说很特别，因为我们从未在环球影业的实际场地拍摄过任何东西，

128
00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:21.670
even though we were an NBC Universal show.
尽管我们是NBC环球旗下的节目。

129
00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:22.710
Yeah.
是啊。

130
00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:23.290
Yeah.
没错。

131
00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:29.150
You know, the name Sid and Dexter's, the reason we called it that, there's a special reason.
你知道，“西德与德克斯特”这个名字，我们之所以这么叫，是有特殊原因的。

132
00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:31.790
Matt sent in an audio clip about that, too.
马特也发来了一段关于此事的音频片段。

133
00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:40.490
On a fun side note, the Dave and Buster's was renamed Sid and Dexter's after my kids.
顺便提个趣事，戴夫与巴斯特餐厅是以我孩子们的名字重新命名为“西德与德克斯特”的。

134
00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:45.590
It was a pitch that I had made to the writers that they seemed to like.
这是我向编剧们提的一个点子，他们似乎很喜欢。

135
00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:56.030
Like, I'm not sure the name actually made it into the show, but I have a Sid and Dexter's sign hanging up in my office from the episode.
