Oh.
噢。

779
00:34:30.680 --> 00:34:33.620
We shot this on February 24th, 2010.
我们是在2010年2月24日拍摄的。

780
00:34:34.480 --> 00:34:37.120
February is a very rainy month in Los Angeles.
二月在洛杉矶是个多雨的月份。

781
00:34:38.080 --> 00:34:42.980
Also, in the background, you can see the parking structure for the Universal Studios tour.
另外，在背景里，你可以看到环球影城游览车的停车楼。

782
00:34:44.420 --> 00:34:45.800
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

783
00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:46.880
Have you ever done it?
你坐过那个游览车吗？

784
00:34:47.140 --> 00:34:47.620
Yes.
坐过。

785
00:34:47.780 --> 00:34:48.140
Me too.
我也坐过。

786
00:34:48.380 --> 00:34:49.100
So fun.
很有趣。

787
00:34:49.660 --> 00:34:51.200
Have they updated it?
他们更新过内容吗？

788
00:34:51.360 --> 00:34:55.700
Because when I did it, it was like Jaws and Back to the Future.
因为我坐的时候，还是《大白鲨》和《回到未来》那些。

789
00:34:56.260 --> 00:34:56.560
Same.
我也是。

790
00:34:56.700 --> 00:34:57.820
And The Psycho House.
还有《惊魂记》里的那栋房子。

791
00:34:57.980 --> 00:34:58.240
Right.
没错。

792
00:34:58.420 --> 00:34:58.600
Yeah.
是啊。

793
00:34:58.820 --> 00:35:01.100
The old lady in the rocking chair up in the window.
窗户边那个坐在摇椅上的老太太。

794
00:35:01.220 --> 00:35:01.400
Yeah.
是啊。

795
00:35:01.500 --> 00:35:01.720
Yeah.
没错。

796
00:35:01.900 --> 00:35:02.600
I don't know.
我不知道。

797
00:35:03.200 --> 00:35:04.320
Surely it's been updated.
肯定更新过了吧。

798
00:35:04.780 --> 00:35:07.160
With movies that are more timely.
换成更时兴的电影了。

799
00:35:07.500 --> 00:35:07.660
Right.
没错。

800
00:35:07.660 --> 00:35:07.720
Right.
确实。

801
00:35:08.060 --> 00:35:10.080
I think Jaws still comes at you, though.
不过我觉得大白鲨还是会向你袭来。

802
00:35:10.220 --> 00:35:10.700
Right, right.
对，没错。

803
00:35:10.780 --> 00:35:11.680
You got to love the Jaws.
你一定会喜欢大白鲨的。

804
00:35:11.720 --> 00:35:15.440
You're going across what looks like a pond, and then Jaws comes at you.
你正穿过看起来像池塘的地方，然后大白鲨就向你袭来了。

805
00:35:15.440 --> 00:35:16.480
It's so fun.
太有意思了。

806
00:35:17.140 --> 00:35:21.940
Well, as everyone is arriving, they walk past the bouncer into the bar.
大家到达时，会经过保镖走进酒吧。

807
00:35:21.940 --> 00:35:24.120
You can see the Sid and Dexter sign.
你可以看到“希德与德克斯特”的招牌。

808
00:35:24.500 --> 00:35:24.880
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

809
00:35:24.880 --> 00:35:28.980
And in the deleted scenes, there was a montage of people arriving.
在删减片段里，有一段人们陆续到达的蒙太奇。

810
00:35:29.300 --> 00:35:33.100
Kevin and Meredith walk in, and they cannot believe that Oscar is there.
凯文和梅雷迪斯走进来，他们简直不敢相信奥斯卡也在那儿。

811
00:35:33.440 --> 00:35:34.920
They say he's a snob.
他们说他是个势利眼。

812
00:35:35.040 --> 00:35:36.100
It's in the deleted scenes.
这在删减片段里。

813
00:35:36.320 --> 00:35:37.940
Here's how Oscar defends himself.
这是奥斯卡为自己辩解的方式。

814
00:35:39.740 --> 00:35:40.840
I'm not a snob.
我不是势利眼。

815
00:35:41.160 --> 00:35:42.480
I hate the opera.
我讨厌歌剧。

816
00:35:43.740 --> 00:35:45.520
Well, the Philadelphia opera.
好吧，是费城歌剧院的歌剧。

817
00:35:46.500 --> 00:35:46.900
Yikes.
哎哟。

818
00:35:49.360 --> 00:35:53.940
He defends himself on being a snob by listing what opera he is not a fan of.
他通过列举自己不喜欢哪种歌剧来为自己不是势利眼辩护。

819
00:35:54.640 --> 00:35:58.220
Then there was a deleted scene as Angela Martin arrives.
然后还有一段安吉拉·马丁到达的删减片段。

820
00:35:58.380 --> 00:35:59.480
She's very dolled up.
她打扮得非常精致。

821
00:35:59.900 --> 00:36:04.240
This was one of my favorite scenes to shoot because it had really silly busy work.
这是我最喜欢拍摄的场景之一，因为里面有一些非常傻的琐事。

822
00:36:04.600 --> 00:36:08.000
The bouncer has asked for her ID, and here it is.
保镖管她要身份证，结果她拿出来了。

823
00:36:08.980 --> 00:36:09.740
Good evening.
晚上好。

824
00:36:09.960 --> 00:36:10.700
Hey, you're fine.
嘿，不用了，你可以进。

825
00:36:11.080 --> 00:36:13.140
No, I have my ID here somewhere.
不，我的身份证就在这儿某处。

826
00:36:13.600 --> 00:36:14.880
Oh, no, you're fine.
噢，不用，你没问题的。

827
00:36:15.220 --> 00:36:16.640
No, you need it.
不，你需要看它的。

828
00:36:16.640 --> 00:36:17.480
That's the rule.
这是规定。

829
00:36:19.060 --> 00:36:19.940
Do with it.
照做吧。

830
00:36:20.820 --> 00:36:21.260
No.
不。

831
00:36:21.520 --> 00:36:23.820
You always know where it is, and then when you need it, you don't.
你总知道它在哪儿，可当你需要它的时候，却找不到了。

832
00:36:23.920 --> 00:36:24.180
You know?
你懂吗？

833
00:36:24.400 --> 00:36:25.160
That happens.
常有的事。

834
00:36:28.830 --> 00:36:29.810
Oh, coupon.
噢，优惠券。

835
00:36:36.890 --> 00:36:39.970
It is almost a minute of me going through my purse.
那段我翻包的戏足足有一分钟长。

836
00:36:41.050 --> 00:36:47.590
I'm pulling out tissues, coupons, all kinds of things, and the bouncer's like, you're fine.
我掏出纸巾、优惠券，各种各样的东西，保镖说，你没问题的。

837
00:36:47.710 --> 00:36:48.450
I'm like, no, no, no.
我说，不，不，不。

838
00:36:48.630 --> 00:36:49.050
No, no.
不，不。

839
00:36:49.370 --> 00:36:53.150
It was so much fun to shoot, but I get why it couldn't make it in.
拍摄过程非常有趣，但我明白为什么它没能入选。

840
00:36:53.230 --> 00:36:54.130
The episode's already long.
这一集已经很长了。

841
00:36:54.130 --> 00:36:56.410
You don't need a minute of me going through my purse.
不需要花一分钟看我翻包。

842
00:36:56.570 --> 00:36:58.330
But those are like my favorite moments.
但那些可是我最喜欢的时刻。

843
00:36:58.670 --> 00:36:59.610
Well, I disagree.
嗯，我不同意。

844
00:36:59.830 --> 00:37:04.390
I would love nothing more than to see one minute of Angela emptying her purse because
我最想看的就是安吉拉花一分钟清空她的包，因为

845
00:37:04.390 --> 00:37:06.290
I'd like to know what she keeps in her purse.
我想知道她包里都装了些什么。

846
00:37:06.430 --> 00:37:07.870
I find those details fascinating.
我觉得这些细节很有趣。

847
00:37:07.870 --> 00:37:09.690
Well, a lot of tissues and coupons.
嗯，很多纸巾和优惠券。

848
00:37:10.250 --> 00:37:13.830
Well, now Pam and Jim are going to invite Michael to play pool with them.
好了，现在帕姆和吉姆要邀请迈克尔和他们一起打台球了。

849
00:37:14.370 --> 00:37:15.650
They need a fourth.
他们需要第四个人。

850
00:37:16.310 --> 00:37:19.530
That's because the third person in the group is the friend.
那是因为他们三人组里的第三个人是那个朋友。

851
00:37:19.830 --> 00:37:20.150
Yeah.
是啊。

852
00:37:20.530 --> 00:37:21.830
And they want to make an introduction.
而且他们想做个介绍。

853
00:37:22.190 --> 00:37:25.410
Also, at this time, Oscar is noting that Matt is not there.
另外，此时奥斯卡注意到马特不在。

854
00:37:25.710 --> 00:37:25.990
No.
没有。

855
00:37:26.470 --> 00:37:27.850
It's sort of a bummer.
这真让人扫兴。

856
00:37:27.990 --> 00:37:29.630
He keeps eyeing the door.
他不停地盯着门口看。

857
00:37:29.810 --> 00:37:31.970
The whole reason for this whole night.
这可是今晚整场活动的全部意义所在。

858
00:37:31.970 --> 00:37:32.050
Right.
没错。

859
00:37:33.510 --> 00:37:33.990
Yes.
是的。

860
00:37:34.510 --> 00:37:37.270
Michael is going to hit it off with Pam's friend, Julie.
迈克尔要和帕姆的朋友朱莉看对眼了。

861
00:37:37.830 --> 00:37:39.870
Yeah, they're really getting along great.
是啊，他们真的相处得很好。

862
00:37:40.070 --> 00:37:41.430
I mean, Julie laughs at everything.
我是说，朱莉对什么都笑。

863
00:37:41.730 --> 00:37:42.050
Yes.
是的。

864
00:37:42.210 --> 00:37:43.310
So Michael is happy.
所以迈克尔很高兴。

865
00:37:43.610 --> 00:37:44.630
Guest star alert.
客串明星预警。

866
00:37:44.870 --> 00:37:47.290
Julie was played by Lori Naughton-Oken.
朱莉由洛里·诺顿-奥肯饰演。

867
00:37:47.610 --> 00:37:49.690
She has been on Friends, Samantha Who.
她曾出演过《老友记》和《第二人生》。

868
00:37:49.810 --> 00:37:52.490
She's a big Groundlings person, and you knew her, right, Ange?
她是“接地气”剧团的资深成员，你认识她，对吧，安吉？

869
00:37:52.570 --> 00:37:52.870
Yes.
是的。

870
00:37:52.870 --> 00:37:54.730
I did a sketch comedy show with her.
我和她一起演过小品喜剧。

871
00:37:54.890 --> 00:37:58.390
She had written this show, and I played a small part in it called Balls Out.
她写了这部剧，我在里面演了一个叫《全力以赴》的小角色。

872
00:37:58.670 --> 00:37:58.990
Ooh.
噢。

873
00:37:58.990 --> 00:38:01.350
I know, and it was a really fun show.
我知道，那是一部非常有趣的剧。

874
00:38:01.610 --> 00:38:03.230
Well, there's going to be another guest star.
嗯，还有另一位客串明星。

875
00:38:03.770 --> 00:38:06.890
It is Isabel, played by Kellen Coleman.
是伊莎贝尔，由凯伦·科尔曼饰演。

876
00:38:07.150 --> 00:38:10.030
She's back, and she's come to the bar as well.
她回来了，也来到了酒吧。

877
00:38:10.350 --> 00:38:11.230
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

878
00:38:11.290 --> 00:38:16.470
She's going to say hi to Pam and then maybe mingle, which means go find Dwight.
她会先跟帕姆打招呼，然后可能会去社交，也就是去找德怀特。

879
00:38:16.610 --> 00:38:17.110
That's right.
没错。

880
00:38:17.530 --> 00:38:22.570
At 7 minutes 57 seconds, you might notice Angela's bright red lipstick.
在7分57秒时，你可能会注意到安吉拉涂了鲜红色的口红。

881
00:38:23.550 --> 00:38:28.270
BJ shared on the commentary that he really wanted Angela to seem like she had tried to go
BJ在评论音轨中分享说，他真的很想让安吉拉看起来像是为了今晚

882
00:38:28.270 --> 00:38:31.310
all out for this evening to get Dwight's attention.
全力以赴，想要引起德怀特的注意。

883
00:38:32.190 --> 00:38:38.450
He wanted her to wear the brightest lipstick that our makeup department had, and he said
他想让她涂上化妆部门能找到的最亮眼的口红，他说

884
00:38:38.450 --> 00:38:41.470
he thought that this is what Angela would think you do.
他认为这就是安吉拉心目中该做的事。

885
00:38:41.630 --> 00:38:45.970
Like, maybe she's seen a soap opera, like how you get your guy, how you go to a bar,
就像，也许她看过肥皂剧，知道怎么去追男人，怎么去酒吧，

886
00:38:46.170 --> 00:38:47.710
put on hot red lipstick.
涂上火辣的红唇。

887
00:38:48.070 --> 00:38:53.250
And he also shared that he was bummed because he wanted the lipstick to be even brighter red.
他还分享说他很沮丧，因为他想让口红颜色更红一些。

888
00:38:53.250 --> 00:38:55.650
But that was all the makeup department had.
但那已经是化妆部门所有的存货了。

889
00:38:56.090 --> 00:38:57.290
Wow, even brighter.
哇，还要更红。

890
00:38:57.530 --> 00:38:57.810
Yeah.
是啊。

891
00:38:57.930 --> 00:38:59.410
It really stands out already.
现在看起来已经很显眼了。

892
00:38:59.590 --> 00:39:00.230
I know.
我知道。

893
00:39:00.630 --> 00:39:06.190
Well, Pam's friend Julie is going to have a talking head where it's clear she kind of likes Michael.
嗯，帕姆的朋友朱莉会有一个采访镜头，很明显她有点喜欢迈克尔。

894
00:39:06.710 --> 00:39:07.050
Yeah.
是啊。

895
00:39:07.610 --> 00:39:10.510
We had a fan catch from Corin F.
我们收到了一位来自俄亥俄州哥伦布市的粉丝科林·F的反馈，他说，

896
00:39:10.690 --> 00:39:13.410
in Columbus, Ohio, who says,
他说，

897
00:39:13.410 --> 00:39:18.590
Starting at 8 minutes 52 seconds, when Pam's friend is doing her talking head about Michael,
从8分52秒开始，当帕姆的朋友在谈论迈克尔时，

898
00:39:18.930 --> 00:39:22.070
you can see Jim laughing at something Pam said.
你可以看到吉姆在笑帕姆说的某句话。

899
00:39:22.430 --> 00:39:27.030
Was this a genuine reaction to something Jenna said, or was this planned?
这是对珍娜所说内容的真实反应，还是预先安排好的？

900
00:39:27.350 --> 00:39:28.130
Are they acting?
他们是在演戏吗？

901
00:39:28.450 --> 00:39:30.730
Either way, it's a very cute background moment.
不管怎样，那都是个非常可爱的背景瞬间。

902
00:39:31.070 --> 00:39:33.090
I think it's just you two in the background.
我觉得背景里只有你们俩。

903
00:39:33.470 --> 00:39:34.390
Oh, no.
噢，不。

904
00:39:34.530 --> 00:39:37.210
This is 100% us in the background.
这百分之百是我们俩在背景里。

905
00:39:37.450 --> 00:39:38.370
Just chatting.
只是在聊天。

906
00:39:38.370 --> 00:39:43.190
Well, I'm very proud because I've clearly said something that has made John noodle.
好吧，我感到非常自豪，因为我显然说了什么话，让约翰笑得像根面条一样。

907
00:39:44.570 --> 00:39:45.950
The noodle laugh.
面条式大笑。

908
00:39:45.950 --> 00:39:46.390
I know.
我知道。

909
00:39:46.390 --> 00:39:52.210
He totally turns into this gelatinous thing that flops around when he's really tickled.
他被逗乐的时候，整个人完全变成了一团软绵绵、瘫来瘫去的东西。

910
00:39:52.410 --> 00:39:52.850
Yes.
没错。

911
00:39:53.030 --> 00:39:54.290
I don't know what I said.
我不知道我说了什么。

912
00:39:54.710 --> 00:39:55.930
Steve is there as well.
史蒂夫也在那儿。

913
00:39:56.030 --> 00:39:57.690
But I'm very proud.
但我感到非常自豪。

914
00:39:57.690 --> 00:39:58.850
I'm clearly hilarious.
我显然很幽默。

915
00:39:59.210 --> 00:40:00.830
And there it is in the background.
看，就在背景里。

916
00:40:01.150 --> 00:40:02.510
Proof of funny.
搞笑的证据。

917
00:40:02.750 --> 00:40:03.370
Thank you.
谢谢。

918
00:40:03.370 --> 00:40:07.490
We also got a fan question from both Kyle T.
我们还收到了来自德克萨斯州休斯顿的凯尔·T.

919
00:40:07.650 --> 00:40:09.530
in Houston, Texas, and Alana D.
和加拿大安大略省的阿兰娜·D.

920
00:40:09.750 --> 00:40:10.970
from Ontario, Canada.
的粉丝提问。

921
00:40:11.390 --> 00:40:12.530
They ask,
他们问，

922
00:40:12.970 --> 00:40:15.650
Why does Pam keep trying to set up Michael?
为什么帕姆一直试图给迈克尔牵线搭桥？

923
00:40:15.850 --> 00:40:17.630
It didn't work with her landlady.
她给房东介绍的时候就没成功。

924
00:40:17.770 --> 00:40:19.410
And look how he treated her mom.
而且看看他是怎么对待她妈妈的。

925
00:40:20.110 --> 00:40:20.690
Why?
为什么呢？

926
00:40:21.430 --> 00:40:22.830
That's very valid.
这问题问得很有道理。

927
00:40:23.250 --> 00:40:24.150
Very valid.
非常有道理。

928
00:40:24.370 --> 00:40:29.250
She has clearly forgotten something has happened to her while she's on maternity leave.
她显然是忘了自己在休产假期间发生过什么事了。

929
00:40:29.330 --> 00:40:30.250
She has mom brain.
她有“妈妈脑”。

930
00:40:30.510 --> 00:40:31.630
I guess so.
我想是吧。

931
00:40:31.630 --> 00:40:34.350
You know when you're tired and you're up all night and you're just like,
你知道当你很累，整晚没睡，然后你就会觉得，

932
00:40:34.530 --> 00:40:36.290
Oh, yeah, that sounds great.
噢，好啊，听起来不错。

933
00:40:36.610 --> 00:40:37.090
I don't know.
我不知道。

934
00:40:37.170 --> 00:40:40.750
I think mom brain also sometimes gives you just like an optimism.
我觉得“妈妈脑”有时也会给你带来一种乐观情绪。

935
00:40:41.110 --> 00:40:41.510
Yes.
是的。

936
00:40:41.850 --> 00:40:44.610
That is, I don't know.
就是，我不知道。

937
00:40:44.970 --> 00:40:45.970
You suddenly.
你突然间。

938
00:40:46.450 --> 00:40:47.890
You want to see the good in people.
你想要看到人们好的一面。

939
00:40:48.050 --> 00:40:48.810
Yes, exactly.
没错，正是这样。

940
00:40:49.170 --> 00:40:51.350
You have this newfound empathy and optimism.
你拥有了这种新发现的同理心和乐观精神。

941
00:40:52.350 --> 00:40:53.470
And compassion.
还有同情心。

942
00:40:53.970 --> 00:40:54.190
Yeah.
是啊。

943
00:40:54.370 --> 00:40:54.490
Yeah.
是啊。

944
00:40:54.890 --> 00:40:56.950
But unfortunately, it's not going to go well.
但不幸的是，这不会有什么好结果。

945
00:40:57.870 --> 00:41:01.170
It might have if Jim hadn't spilled the beans.
如果吉姆没有说漏嘴的话，或许会有好结果。

946
00:41:01.710 --> 00:41:02.130
I know.
我知道。

947
00:41:02.290 --> 00:41:04.910
If Jim would have just let Michael keep being himself.
如果吉姆当时只是让迈克尔继续做他自己就好了。

948
00:41:04.910 --> 00:41:07.810
But Jim said, yeah, I guess Pam was right.
但吉姆说了，是啊，我想帕姆是对的。

949
00:41:08.250 --> 00:41:10.530
You know, you guys are hitting it off.
你知道，你们俩相处得挺好。

