His grandfather had one.
他祖父有一顶。

1022
00:44:25.600 --> 00:44:27.620
I mean, I have to think he has more now.
我是说，我觉得他现在肯定不止这个数了。

1023
00:44:28.460 --> 00:44:31.680
Since 2022, do you think his wife let him add to it?
从2022年算起，你觉得他妻子会让他继续买吗？

1024
00:44:31.740 --> 00:44:32.140
Maybe.
也许吧。

1025
00:44:32.360 --> 00:44:36.600
Maybe it's like the thing where you add one but take one away, so you get new stuff.
也许就像那种买一顶扔一顶的模式，这样就能不断换新。

1026
00:44:36.820 --> 00:44:37.120
Right.
没错。

1027
00:44:37.700 --> 00:44:43.060
There was quite a bit of debate in the writer's room about the difference in regular Mike and date Mike.
编剧室里曾就“普通迈克”和“约会迈克”的区别进行过相当激烈的讨论。

1028
00:44:43.440 --> 00:44:43.700
Okay.
好的。

1029
00:44:43.700 --> 00:44:46.220
BJ talked about it on the DVD commentary.
BJ在DVD评论音轨里提到过这件事。

1030
00:44:46.660 --> 00:44:52.840
He said there were pitches to make date Mike even bigger and his clothes more extravagant.
他说当时有人提议让“约会迈克”的形象更夸张，衣服更花哨。

1031
00:44:53.020 --> 00:44:59.000
Like, in one pitch, they had him wearing a dragon t-shirt or some Ed Hardy clothes.
比如，有人提议让他穿一件印有龙的T恤，或者穿些Ed Hardy品牌的衣服。

1032
00:44:59.160 --> 00:45:04.460
But Steve said he thought it was less of a wardrobe change and more of a personality change.
但史蒂夫说他认为这不应该仅仅是服装上的改变，更应该是性格上的转变。

1033
00:45:04.880 --> 00:45:07.520
So, they went with a Kangol hat.
所以，他们最终选了那顶康格尔帽。

1034
00:45:07.520 --> 00:45:09.020
Well, I loved it.
嗯，我超爱那个造型。

1035
00:45:09.240 --> 00:45:12.320
When Michael returns, Jim and Pam are surprised.
当迈克尔回来时，吉姆和帕姆都很惊讶。

1036
00:45:12.620 --> 00:45:14.460
They notice the shift right away.
他们立刻注意到了他的变化。

1037
00:45:15.320 --> 00:45:16.940
I improvised the line,
那句台词是我即兴发挥的，

1038
00:45:17.460 --> 00:45:19.040
Why are you wearing a hat now?
你现在为什么戴着帽子？

1039
00:45:20.280 --> 00:45:24.940
So, I looked at the table draft, like you said, Angela, and originally he had changed his shirt.
所以，安吉拉，正如你所说，我看了剧本初稿，原本他是换了件衬衫的。

1040
00:45:25.160 --> 00:45:27.220
And Pam had a line where she said,
帕姆当时有一句台词是说，

1041
00:45:27.300 --> 00:45:28.880
Why are you wearing a different shirt now?
你现在为什么换了件衬衫？

1042
00:45:29.360 --> 00:45:33.740
But then by the shooting draft, that had been taken out, and there was just nothing.
但到了拍摄剧本时，那句台词被删掉了，什么都没剩下。

1043
00:45:34.000 --> 00:45:35.480
Pam didn't have a line there.
帕姆在那儿没词了。

1044
00:45:35.600 --> 00:45:39.200
But I think I must have remembered that shirt line, which made me laugh.
但我猜我一定还记得那句关于衬衫的台词，这让我觉得很好笑。

1045
00:45:39.300 --> 00:45:41.620
And so, I added, Why are you wearing a hat now?
于是我加了一句：“你现在为什么戴着帽子？”

1046
00:45:42.100 --> 00:45:43.320
Well, I loved it.
嗯，我超爱那个造型。

1047
00:45:43.620 --> 00:45:45.560
I loved Pam and Jim's reaction.
我特别喜欢帕姆和吉姆的反应。

1048
00:45:45.760 --> 00:45:48.200
They know now everything's going to go south.
他们知道接下来一切都要搞砸了。

1049
00:45:48.900 --> 00:45:50.740
Michael has this big swagger.
迈克尔当时那副趾高气扬的样子。

1050
00:45:51.020 --> 00:45:53.380
He's spinning this pool stick around.
他还在那儿转着台球杆。

1051
00:45:53.380 --> 00:45:58.240
At 9 minutes, 40 seconds, when Michael shoots the pool ball and it goes flying at you guys.
在9分40秒时，迈克尔击球，台球朝你们飞了过去。

1052
00:45:58.420 --> 00:45:58.620
Yes.
是的。

1053
00:45:58.780 --> 00:46:02.820
Matt Soane shared that Steve really did that, and thankfully, they got it in the first take.
马特·索恩分享说，那是史蒂夫真的打出来的，谢天谢地，他们一次就拍成了。

1054
00:46:02.980 --> 00:46:03.800
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1055
00:46:03.960 --> 00:46:04.240
Yeah.
是啊。

1056
00:46:04.580 --> 00:46:06.040
I didn't remember that.
我不记得了。

1057
00:46:07.360 --> 00:46:08.960
You guys ducked for real.
你们当时是真的躲开了。

1058
00:46:11.380 --> 00:46:16.600
Well, meanwhile, Kelly and Ryan are about to finish an intense round of their dance game.
嗯，与此同时，凯利和瑞安正要结束他们那场激烈的跳舞机游戏。

