You have no brothers.
你也不怎么喝酒，

1098
00:47:46.780 --> 00:47:48.680
You're not much of a drinker.
你是怎么做到打扑克和台球都这么厉害的？

1099
00:47:48.940 --> 00:47:52.120
How are you so good at poker and pool?
我也有同样的疑问。

1100
00:47:53.020 --> 00:47:54.720
I have the same question.
我也想问这个问题。

1101
00:47:55.960 --> 00:47:58.640
When I was in high school, my friend Stacy and I,
我上高中的时候，我和我的朋友斯泰西，

1102
00:47:58.800 --> 00:48:02.000
by the way, Stacy, the inventor of the tan baster.
顺便说一下，斯泰西就是那个美黑喷雾的发明者。

1103
00:48:02.180 --> 00:48:02.560
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1104
00:48:02.780 --> 00:48:07.240
The two of us in high school, we got a little obsessed with pool
我们俩上高中时，对台球有点着迷，

1105
00:48:07.240 --> 00:48:10.940
after we watched the movies The Hustler and The Color of Money.
在看了《江湖浪子》和《金钱本色》这两部电影之后。

1106
00:48:10.940 --> 00:48:11.740
Paul Newman.
保罗·纽曼。

1107
00:48:12.080 --> 00:48:12.500
Yeah.
没错。

1108
00:48:12.900 --> 00:48:13.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1109
00:48:13.460 --> 00:48:14.480
Those sweet blue eyes.
那双迷人的蓝眼睛。

1110
00:48:14.680 --> 00:48:16.420
So you watched these movies, and then you were like,
所以你们看了这些电影，然后就觉得，

1111
00:48:16.460 --> 00:48:17.360
I'm going to learn pool?
我要去学打台球？

1112
00:48:17.560 --> 00:48:17.800
Yeah.
对。

1113
00:48:17.980 --> 00:48:20.060
We went to a pool hall in Kirkwood, Missouri,
我们去了密苏里州柯克伍德的一家台球厅，

1114
00:48:20.960 --> 00:48:23.700
and we learned how to play pool.
然后学会了怎么打台球。

1115
00:48:24.240 --> 00:48:27.600
And our plan was that we were going to go on the road,
我们的计划是去各地巡回，

1116
00:48:27.660 --> 00:48:29.060
and we were going to hustle people.
去赢别人的钱。

1117
00:48:29.300 --> 00:48:32.980
This was our grand plan to become pool hustlers.
这就是我们成为台球赌徒的宏伟计划。

1118
00:48:33.920 --> 00:48:35.860
So when you weren't playing field hockey,
所以当你不打曲棍球的时候，

1119
00:48:37.220 --> 00:48:39.140
we were going to be professional pool hustlers.
我们就要去当职业台球赌徒了。

1120
00:48:39.380 --> 00:48:39.840
Professional hustlers.
职业赌徒。

1121
00:48:40.040 --> 00:48:40.220
Okay.
好吧。

1122
00:48:40.720 --> 00:48:42.040
We got very good.
我们变得非常厉害。

1123
00:48:42.340 --> 00:48:43.480
I believe it.
我相信。

1124
00:48:43.660 --> 00:48:46.600
And I really enjoyed this episode because it was my chance
我真的很喜欢这一集，因为这是我机会，

1125
00:48:46.600 --> 00:48:49.260
to kind of show off some of my skills.
可以展示一下我的球技。

1126
00:48:49.640 --> 00:48:52.360
My husband's very good at pool, and he wants a pool table.
我丈夫台球打得很好，他想要一张台球桌。

1127
00:48:52.580 --> 00:48:52.940
Oh.
哦。

1128
00:48:52.940 --> 00:48:53.420
I'm like, what?
我说，什么？

1129
00:48:53.520 --> 00:48:55.080
So we're not going to have a dining table,
所以我们不打算要餐桌了，

1130
00:48:55.160 --> 00:48:56.160
so you're going to have a pool table?
你要买张台球桌？

1131
00:48:56.260 --> 00:48:57.380
I'll be over all the time.
那我以后会经常过去玩的。

1132
00:48:57.480 --> 00:48:58.540
Well, it might happen.
嗯，这事儿没准真会发生。

1133
00:48:59.100 --> 00:49:02.220
Oh, I want to say something about this arcade dance game.
哦，关于这个街机跳舞游戏，我想说点什么。

1134
00:49:02.640 --> 00:49:05.720
Would you be surprised to know that they are not playing
如果我告诉你他们玩的不是

1135
00:49:05.720 --> 00:49:06.800
Dance Dance Revolution?
《跳舞机》（Dance Dance Revolution），你会惊讶吗？

1136
00:49:08.020 --> 00:49:10.520
I feel like this is, like, a leading question.
我觉得你这是在诱导我回答。

1137
00:49:10.520 --> 00:49:11.680
I don't know the answer.
我不知道答案。

1138
00:49:12.500 --> 00:49:15.180
That's the only game I know of with the feet, the thing.
那是唯一我知道的用脚踩的游戏。

1139
00:49:15.460 --> 00:49:15.880
Me too.
我也是。

1140
00:49:16.000 --> 00:49:16.380
Yeah, that's it.
没错，就是那个。

1141
00:49:16.420 --> 00:49:16.760
Okay.
好吧。

1142
00:49:17.180 --> 00:49:17.780
Okay, no.
好吧，不是。

1143
00:49:17.780 --> 00:49:19.280
Oh, there's another one.
哦，还有另一个。

1144
00:49:19.460 --> 00:49:20.920
It's called Pump It Up.
它叫《Pump It Up》。

1145
00:49:20.920 --> 00:49:24.820
It is the other music video game dance series.
它是另一个音乐视频舞蹈游戏系列。

1146
00:49:24.820 --> 00:49:27.640
It's by a Korean arcade game producer.
它是由一家韩国街机游戏制作商开发的。

1147
00:49:28.040 --> 00:49:31.560
The original version of the game was released in South Korea
该游戏的最初版本于1999年8月

1148
00:49:31.560 --> 00:49:33.160
in August of 1999.
在韩国发行。

1149
00:49:34.220 --> 00:49:35.380
Here's the difference.
区别就在这里。

1150
00:49:36.060 --> 00:49:39.480
Dance Dance Revolution only has four squares that you can step on,
《跳舞机》只有四个可以踩的方块，

1151
00:49:39.620 --> 00:49:41.400
and they're in, like, a plus sign.
它们就像是一个加号的形状。

1152
00:49:41.620 --> 00:49:41.760
Yeah.
没错。

1153
00:49:42.280 --> 00:49:45.260
Pump It Up has five things you can press on.
《Pump It Up》上有五个你可以踩的按键。

1154
00:49:45.400 --> 00:49:49.500
You can press the middle square, and then it makes, like, an X.
你可以踩中间的方块，然后它会形成一个叉的形状。

1155
00:49:49.760 --> 00:49:50.040
Yeah.
没错。

1156
00:49:50.040 --> 00:49:51.380
I took screen grabs.
我截了图。

1157
00:49:52.000 --> 00:49:53.040
I mom-detectived it.
我发挥了妈妈的侦探本能去调查了。

1158
00:49:53.740 --> 00:49:55.520
And it's not Dance Dance Revolution.
那不是《跳舞机》（Dance Dance Revolution）。

1159
00:49:55.740 --> 00:49:56.300
It's Pump It Up.
那是《Pump It Up》。

1160
00:49:57.460 --> 00:49:59.400
That's what they're playing, and they had to bring it in.
他们玩的就是这个，而且他们还得专门把它搬进来。

1161
00:49:59.560 --> 00:50:01.300
I know this happens later in the episode,
我知道这事儿发生在这一集的后面，

1162
00:50:01.400 --> 00:50:04.960
but when you see Creed dancing on that thing, he really was.
但当你看到克里德在上面跳舞时，他是真的在跳。

1163
00:50:05.180 --> 00:50:07.920
And we did a bunch of takes, and I remember we were like,
我们拍了很多条，我记得当时我们说，

1164
00:50:07.980 --> 00:50:09.720
wait, I think Creed's, like, getting lightheaded.
等等，我觉得克里德好像有点头晕了。

1165
00:50:09.880 --> 00:50:10.840
We need to give him a break.
我们需要让他休息一下。

1166
00:50:11.080 --> 00:50:12.820
He's been dancing for a long time.
他已经跳了很久了。

1167
00:50:13.040 --> 00:50:15.720
Yeah, when I was trading messages with Matt, he was like,
是啊，我和马特发消息的时候，他说，

1168
00:50:15.720 --> 00:50:21.260
I think we almost killed Creed because he did so many takes of the dancing game.
我觉得我们差点把克里德给累坏了，因为他拍了太多次跳舞机的镜头。

1169
00:50:21.260 --> 00:50:22.920
And he was going all out.
而且他还是全力以赴地跳。

1170
00:50:23.500 --> 00:50:27.800
Randy said that they also had a graphic made, and you don't see it in the episode,
兰迪说他们还专门做了一个画面，虽然你在剧集里没看到，

1171
00:50:28.080 --> 00:50:33.100
but it shows that Creed has all of the top 10 high scores on the leaderboard.
但上面显示克里德霸占了排行榜前十名的所有高分。

1172
00:50:34.000 --> 00:50:34.820
That's awesome.
那太棒了。

1173
00:50:35.080 --> 00:50:38.840
And I guess the reason they did all that was because originally the tag to this episode
我想他们之所以做这些，是因为这一集的结尾彩蛋原本

1174
00:50:38.840 --> 00:50:42.880
was going to be Creed on the Dance Machine, and you see that he's like Dance Master.
设定是克里德在跳舞机上，你会看到他简直就是跳舞大师。

1175
00:50:43.060 --> 00:50:44.460
With a crowd around him.
周围还围着一群人。

1176
00:50:44.760 --> 00:50:46.260
But then they moved it to the middle of the episode.
但后来他们把它移到了剧集中间。

1177
00:50:46.560 --> 00:50:51.480
Coming up next is probably my most famous meme that I'm a part of.
接下来要出现的可能是我参与过的最著名的表情包了。

1178
00:50:51.940 --> 00:50:52.380
What?
什么？

1179
00:50:52.760 --> 00:50:53.160
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1180
00:50:53.400 --> 00:50:55.120
No, there are more famous memes.
不，还有更出名的表情包。

1181
00:50:55.220 --> 00:50:56.140
No, not for me.
不，对我来说不是。

1182
00:50:56.540 --> 00:50:57.100
Come on.
得了吧。

1183
00:50:57.100 --> 00:50:58.080
I am telling you.
我跟你说真的。

1184
00:50:58.460 --> 00:51:00.720
For real, this is the most famous meme I'm in.
真的，这就是我参与过的最著名的表情包。

1185
00:51:00.920 --> 00:51:04.360
Like, they will take this moment where Angela sneaks up on Dwight,
就是，他们会截取安吉拉悄悄走到德怀特身后的那一刻，

1186
00:51:04.900 --> 00:51:06.640
and, you know, they'll caption it.
然后，你知道的，给它配上字幕。

1187
00:51:06.640 --> 00:51:09.540
It's someone reacting to something that scares the crap out of them,
那是某人对吓坏自己的事情做出的反应，

1188
00:51:09.620 --> 00:51:10.780
and they drop the F-bomb.
然后他们会爆粗口。

1189
00:51:10.920 --> 00:51:14.400
And it's been recycled over and over.
这个素材被反复使用了无数次。

1190
00:51:14.740 --> 00:51:17.620
So, like, over you, they'll write spiders?
所以，比如在你的头上，他们会写上“蜘蛛”？

1191
00:51:17.960 --> 00:51:18.160
Yes.
是的。

1192
00:51:18.160 --> 00:51:21.380
Or they'll write, like, something that is scary.
或者他们会写上一些让人害怕的东西。

1193
00:51:21.460 --> 00:51:22.420
They're phobia, basically.
基本上就是他们的恐惧症。

1194
00:51:22.600 --> 00:51:22.880
Yes.
是的。

1195
00:51:23.060 --> 00:51:25.340
I titled this scene Lurk Much.
我给这一幕起名叫“潜行大师”。

1196
00:51:25.540 --> 00:51:26.620
Should we set it up?
我们要介绍一下背景吗？

1197
00:51:26.740 --> 00:51:27.140
Yes.
好。

1198
00:51:27.640 --> 00:51:31.480
Okay, well, Dwight and Isabel are walking through the arcade.
好的，德怀特和伊莎贝尔正在游乐厅里走着。

1199
00:51:31.740 --> 00:51:32.440
They're flirting.
他们在调情。

1200
00:51:33.300 --> 00:51:33.840
Chatting.
在聊天。

1201
00:51:34.040 --> 00:51:36.540
And Angela, in her bright red lipstick, is juSt...
还有安吉拉，涂着鲜红的口红，简直是……

1202
00:51:36.640 --> 00:51:38.100
All up on their heels.
紧紧跟在他们身后。

1203
00:51:38.420 --> 00:51:40.880
And then, after Isabel walks away,
然后，在伊莎贝尔走开之后，

1204
00:51:41.660 --> 00:51:44.520
Dwight is completely shocked that Angela was standing there,
德怀特对安吉拉站在那里感到非常震惊，

1205
00:51:44.620 --> 00:51:46.120
and has a very large reaction.
并做出了非常夸张的反应。

1206
00:51:46.880 --> 00:51:48.180
Lady, we got mail.
女士们，我们有邮件。

1207
00:51:48.720 --> 00:51:50.640
Fan question from Desi C.
来自德西·C的粉丝提问，

1208
00:51:50.900 --> 00:51:52.600
in Stilwell, Oklahoma.
地点在俄克拉荷马州的斯蒂尔威尔。

1209
00:51:53.400 --> 00:51:57.420
In the scene with Dwight and Isabel walking and Angela following close behind,
在德怀特和伊莎贝尔走路、安吉拉紧随其后的那场戏里，

1210
00:51:57.820 --> 00:52:03.080
Isabel seems to be of equal height to Dwight, making Angela look so small in comparison.
伊莎贝尔看起来和德怀特身高相当，这让安吉拉显得格外娇小。

1211
00:52:03.500 --> 00:52:07.280
Was this done intentionally or just a happy accident?
这是刻意安排的，还是纯属巧合？

1212
00:52:07.580 --> 00:52:14.120
I looked up actress Kellen Coleman, and her height, according to IMDb, is 5'9 1⁄2".
我查了演员凯伦·科尔曼的资料，根据IMDb显示，她身高5英尺9.5英寸。

1213
00:52:14.120 --> 00:52:17.920
But standing next to Rain, she looks almost to be the same height.
但站在雷恩旁边，她看起来几乎和他一样高。

1214
00:52:18.260 --> 00:52:19.620
It was intentional.
这是刻意安排的。

1215
00:52:20.280 --> 00:52:22.380
You know, Rain is 6'3".
你知道，雷恩身高6英尺3英寸。

1216
00:52:22.380 --> 00:52:23.820
Kellen is very tall.
凯伦非常高。

1217
00:52:24.300 --> 00:52:26.180
And IMDb 5'1".
而IMDb上说我身高5英尺1英寸。

1218
00:52:26.940 --> 00:52:32.500
Wardrobe purposely for this episode put me in flats to really accentuate the height difference.
这一集的服装组特意让我穿平底鞋，以突出身高差。

1219
00:52:32.720 --> 00:52:34.300
Normally, I wore heels on the show.
通常我在剧中是穿高跟鞋的。

1220
00:52:34.520 --> 00:52:35.520
I'm in flats.
但我穿的是平底鞋。

1221
00:52:36.040 --> 00:52:41.360
BJ also shared it was his idea that only the top of my head would be visible as I walked behind them.
BJ还分享说，是他提议让我走在他们身后时，只露出头顶。

1222
00:52:41.360 --> 00:52:44.700
I went to the shooting draft, and here's how it described the scene.
我查了拍摄剧本，上面是这样描述这场戏的。

1223
00:52:45.460 --> 00:52:49.460
Dwight and Isabel stroll the arcade area, looking for a game to play.
德怀特和伊莎贝尔在游乐区漫步，寻找可以玩的游戏。

1224
00:52:50.040 --> 00:52:53.340
Angela trails behind, only the top of her head in frame.
安吉拉跟在后面，画面里只能看到她的头顶。

1225
00:52:54.100 --> 00:52:54.580
Amazing.
太棒了。

1226
00:52:55.480 --> 00:52:58.660
Well, I will add that I remember Kellen was in heels.
嗯，我还要补充一点，我记得凯伦当时穿了高跟鞋。

1227
00:52:59.020 --> 00:52:59.380
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1228
00:52:59.660 --> 00:53:05.480
They put her in some, like, 3-inch, kind of not wedges, but, like, thick-heeled shoes
他们让她穿了那种大概3英寸高的鞋，不是坡跟，而是粗跟鞋，

1229
00:53:05.480 --> 00:53:08.560
so that she would be super tall compared to you.
这样她和你比起来就会显得特别高。

1230
00:53:09.500 --> 00:53:11.200
We got another fan question.
我们还有另一个粉丝提问。

1231
00:53:11.360 --> 00:53:13.120
From Xenia W.
来自不列颠哥伦比亚省的谢妮亚·W，

1232
00:53:13.360 --> 00:53:14.300
in British Columbia,
她问：

1233
00:53:15.000 --> 00:53:19.300
Dwight looks utterly shocked by the sudden appearance of Angela Martin behind him.
德怀特对安吉拉·马丁突然出现在他身后感到非常震惊。

1234
00:53:19.500 --> 00:53:23.840
His reaction was so genuine, down to the bleeped swear word he dropped.
他的反应非常真实，甚至还爆了句被消音的粗口。

1235
00:53:24.100 --> 00:53:28.760
Was Rainn Wilson not expecting Angela to show up, or was this a scripted moment?
雷恩·威尔逊当时没预料到安吉拉会出现，还是说这是剧本里写好的？

1236
00:53:29.340 --> 00:53:32.180
So, this moment was totally found on the day.
这个瞬间完全是现场发挥的。

1237
00:53:32.560 --> 00:53:34.160
It's not in the shooting draft.
剧本里并没有写。

1238
00:53:34.580 --> 00:53:37.400
BJ shared in the commentary that they pitched it to Rainn,
BJ在评论音轨里分享说，他们向雷恩提议了这个点子，

1239
00:53:37.400 --> 00:53:41.100
and he was reluctant to do it because he thought it might seem too broad.
但他当时很抗拒，觉得这可能显得太夸张了。

1240
00:53:41.460 --> 00:53:43.460
But then they were like, let's just give it a try.
但后来他们说，试一下吧。

1241
00:53:43.580 --> 00:53:44.280
Just give it a try.
就试一下。

1242
00:53:44.580 --> 00:53:49.600
And then I remember they told me to get as close to, like, Rainn's, like, arm,
我记得他们当时让我尽量靠近雷恩的胳膊，

1243
00:53:49.980 --> 00:53:53.000
like, just to sort of be way down there by his elbow.
就像是缩在他手肘旁边一样。

1244
00:53:53.580 --> 00:53:56.740
And so, I was trailing him really closely.
所以我紧紧地跟在他后面。

1245
00:53:57.040 --> 00:53:59.780
And when he turned around, I was right there.
当他转过身时，我就在那儿。

1246
00:54:00.060 --> 00:54:01.800
And it just worked.
效果出奇地好。

1247
00:54:01.800 --> 00:54:03.240
And we all started laughing.
我们所有人都笑了起来。

1248
00:54:03.240 --> 00:54:04.980
We knew we had to do it again.
我们知道必须再拍一次。

1249
00:54:05.620 --> 00:54:06.860
It's so lurky.
这太像跟踪狂了。

1250
00:54:07.000 --> 00:54:07.460
Lurk much?
很会潜行嘛？

1251
00:54:07.800 --> 00:54:08.060
I know.
我知道。

1252
00:54:08.800 --> 00:54:15.040
Well, back over at the pool tables, Michael's going to try to tie a cherry stem with his tongue.
嗯，回到台球桌那边，迈克尔打算试着用舌头打结樱桃梗。

1253
00:54:15.940 --> 00:54:18.060
But instead, he starts choking.
但结果他开始噎住了。

1254
00:54:18.700 --> 00:54:20.420
Jenna, this scene was even bigger.
珍娜，这一幕原本规模更大。

1255
00:54:20.660 --> 00:54:26.140
In the shooting draft, not only does he choke, but then he starts dribbling cherry juice down his shirt.
在拍摄剧本里，他不仅噎住了，还开始让樱桃汁滴到衬衫上。

1256
00:54:26.280 --> 00:54:26.660
So gross.
太恶心了。

1257
00:54:26.900 --> 00:54:31.080
And then he turns to Julie and says, you want to maybe hit a hot tub after this?
然后他转向朱莉说，要不要待会儿去泡个热水澡？

1258
00:54:31.220 --> 00:54:31.880
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1259
00:54:32.860 --> 00:54:38.220
Also, in this scene, he is kind of, like, spinning the pool cue around.
而且在这一幕里，他还在那儿转着台球杆玩。

1260
00:54:38.440 --> 00:54:38.740
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1261
00:54:39.300 --> 00:54:43.880
We had a fan catch from Dandy Y in Canada who says,
我们收到了一位来自加拿大Dandy Y的粉丝留言，他说：

1262
00:54:44.460 --> 00:54:47.980
Fakie pool cue at 12 minutes, 13 seconds.
12分13秒处有假台球杆。

1263
00:54:48.320 --> 00:54:51.460
When Michael is spinning the pool cue, you can see it bending.
当迈克尔转动台球杆时，你能看到它弯了。

1264
00:54:51.820 --> 00:54:53.820
What was it actually made of?
那到底是用什么做的？

1265
00:54:54.000 --> 00:54:55.200
Ooh, good catch.
噢，好眼力。

1266
00:54:55.320 --> 00:54:56.420
Such a good catch.
真是好眼力。

1267
00:54:56.540 --> 00:54:57.800
You really can see it.
你真的能看出来。

1268
00:54:57.900 --> 00:55:00.480
It is 100% a rubber pool cue.
那百分之百是一根橡胶台球杆。

1269
00:55:00.640 --> 00:55:01.500
It is so bendy.
它太软了。

1270
00:55:01.500 --> 00:55:03.220
I mean, it's almost ridiculous.
我是说，简直荒谬。

1271
00:55:03.220 --> 00:55:04.540
I can't believe it made it in.
真不敢相信这居然被剪进正片了。

1272
00:55:05.100 --> 00:55:07.540
Well, there was an alternate Michael talking head.
嗯，当时还有一个迈克尔的备用采访镜头。

1273
00:55:07.540 --> 00:55:09.780
It was in the shooting draft candy bag.
它在拍摄剧本的“糖果袋”里。

1274
00:55:10.100 --> 00:55:11.240
It made me laugh.
它把我逗笑了。

1275
00:55:11.640 --> 00:55:14.700
Michael says, I've been dating for over 30 years.
迈克尔说，我约会都三十多年了。

1276
00:55:14.760 --> 00:55:16.340
I think I know what I'm doing.
我想我知道自己在干什么。

1277
00:55:16.600 --> 00:55:17.160
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1278
00:55:21.400 --> 00:55:24.020
Well, Isabel and Dwight are playing whack-a-mole.
嗯，伊莎贝尔和德怀特在玩打地鼠。

1279
00:55:24.580 --> 00:55:26.280
And Dwight is really good at it.
德怀特玩得特别好。

1280
00:55:26.340 --> 00:55:28.000
And Isabel's like, oh, my gosh, you're so good at it.
伊莎贝尔说，天哪，你玩得真好。

1281
00:55:28.000 --> 00:55:30.460
And then Angela tries to join in, the lurker.
然后安吉拉试图加入，那个潜伏者。

1282
00:55:31.260 --> 00:55:33.520
And she says, this looks like a hoot.
她说，这看起来挺有意思的。

1283
00:55:34.020 --> 00:55:36.580
And you guys, it just made me think of my journal entry, Sam.
伙计们，这让我想起了我的日记条目，山姆。

1284
00:55:37.840 --> 00:55:38.880
This looks like a hoot.
这看起来挺有意思的。

1285
00:55:38.880 --> 00:55:39.940
I think I got tooted.
我觉得我被“嘟”到了。

1286
00:55:40.980 --> 00:55:43.020
You hit these balls with a large stick.
你用一根大棍子去敲这些球。

1287
00:55:43.860 --> 00:55:44.860
Yes, exactly.
是的，没错。

1288
00:55:44.860 --> 00:55:50.620
I want to know how Angela Kinsey would write in her journal about her first whack-a-mole game.
我想知道安吉拉·金赛会怎么在日记里写她第一次玩打地鼠。

1289
00:55:51.120 --> 00:55:52.620
Please, can we have that?
拜托，能给我们念一下吗？

1290
00:55:52.880 --> 00:55:53.620
We need it.
我们需要这个。

1291
00:55:53.700 --> 00:55:54.880
It would go something like this.
大概会是这样写的。

1292
00:55:55.360 --> 00:55:59.680
There was this really interesting machine where little tiny animals came out.
有一台非常有趣的机器，会有小小的动物钻出来。

1293
00:55:59.800 --> 00:56:00.900
And they wanted me to hit them.
它们想让我去打它们。

1294
00:56:00.980 --> 00:56:02.440
And I said, I will not.
我说，我才不干。

1295
00:56:02.440 --> 00:56:04.780
And then I had a Cosmopolitan.
然后我喝了一杯大都会鸡尾酒。

1296
00:56:07.680 --> 00:56:08.160
XOXO.
亲亲抱抱。

1297
00:56:08.260 --> 00:56:14.140
And then I would probably finish my journal entry with, I'll fill you in next time on what happened when I tried skee-ball.
然后我可能会这样结束我的日记：下次再告诉你我尝试玩滚球游戏时发生了什么。

1298
00:56:15.100 --> 00:56:15.580
XOXO.
亲亲抱抱。

1299
00:56:16.060 --> 00:56:16.540
Hugs.
拥抱。

1300
00:56:16.700 --> 00:56:23.080
I love how your journal entries, and this is true about your journal entries, they end with like a cliffhanger.
我喜欢你的日记条目——这一点在你所有的日记里都是真的——它们结尾总是像悬念剧一样。

1301
00:56:23.280 --> 00:56:23.620
Yes.
是的。

1302
00:56:23.800 --> 00:56:28.620
Like, next time, I'm going to give you some details on this other thing.
比如下次，我会给你讲讲关于另一件事的细节。

1303
00:56:28.720 --> 00:56:30.700
Yeah, they all end up like the Gossip Girl ones.
是啊，它们最后都像《绯闻女孩》里的那些一样。

1304
00:56:30.820 --> 00:56:31.200
I know.
我知道。

1305
00:56:32.440 --> 00:56:37.860
And then I also like write in my journal, like I'll say things like, oh, sorry to bore you.
而且我还会写日记，比如我会写些“噢，抱歉让你觉得无聊了”之类的话。

1306
00:56:37.960 --> 00:56:39.060
I've gone on and on.
我真是喋喋不休。

1307
00:56:39.360 --> 00:56:40.340
Who's reading this?
到底谁会看这个？

1308
00:56:40.400 --> 00:56:41.280
Who am I writing to?
我到底是在写给谁看？

1309
00:56:42.040 --> 00:56:44.680
I can't believe I talked that long about whack-a-mole.
真不敢相信我居然说了那么久关于打地鼠的事。

1310
00:56:44.800 --> 00:56:45.680
My bad.
我的错。

1311
00:56:45.920 --> 00:56:46.780
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1312
00:56:46.820 --> 00:56:50.820
Could you do a young adult book series that is just your journals?
你能出一套青少年系列小说，内容全是你写的日记吗？

1313
00:56:51.280 --> 00:56:52.060
Please, no.
求你了，别。

1314
00:56:52.800 --> 00:56:53.500
That would be so weird.
那也太奇怪了。

1315
00:56:53.500 --> 00:56:54.880
I really like this character.
我真的很喜欢这个角色。

1316
00:56:57.980 --> 00:57:00.440
Well, Angela's whack-a-mole is not going to go well.
好吧，安吉拉的打地鼠计划注定要失败了。

1317
00:57:00.960 --> 00:57:02.860
And Dwight pulls her aside and says, you know what?
然后德怀特把她拉到一边说，你知道吗？

1318
00:57:03.480 --> 00:57:05.880
We had a good run, but I want a big family.
我们在一起很开心，但我想要一个大家庭。

1319
00:57:06.000 --> 00:57:07.280
Like, a big, big family.
那种超级大的大家庭。

1320
00:57:07.460 --> 00:57:09.440
And she doesn't need to worry about their contract anymore.
而且她再也不用担心他们的合同了。

1321
00:57:09.740 --> 00:57:10.120
Dissolved.
作废了。

1322
00:57:10.260 --> 00:57:11.980
He tries to break their contract.
他试图撕毁他们的合同。

1323
00:57:12.120 --> 00:57:17.200
How many pieces of identification did they have on that table when they were making this contract?
他们签这份合同时，桌上放了多少证件啊？

1324
00:57:17.300 --> 00:57:18.800
So many signatures and stamps.
签了那么多名，盖了那么多章。

1325
00:57:18.800 --> 00:57:19.660
How dare he?
他怎么敢这样？

1326
00:57:20.280 --> 00:57:20.720
Truly.
真的。

1327
00:57:21.020 --> 00:57:21.340
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1328
00:57:22.420 --> 00:57:23.760
She's not going to take it well.
她肯定不会善罢甘休的。

1329
00:57:24.200 --> 00:57:26.540
Meanwhile, Michael is on top of a pool table.
与此同时，迈克尔正站在台球桌上。

1330
00:57:26.820 --> 00:57:28.560
I don't know what he's doing.
我不知道他在干什么。

1331
00:57:28.700 --> 00:57:31.080
He's playing like air guitar on his pool stick.
他正拿着台球杆在那儿弹空气吉他呢。

1332
00:57:31.460 --> 00:57:34.580
I mean, it's going to get the attention of the manager.
我是说，这肯定会引起经理的注意。

1333
00:57:35.020 --> 00:57:38.140
Yeah, she's like, do you want to pay $400 to refelt this table?
是啊，她说，你想花400美元重新铺台球桌的呢绒布吗？

1334
00:57:38.240 --> 00:57:43.520
And Michael says, yeah, why don't you send the bill to 23 I Don't Care Lane, Scranton, Pennsylvania?
迈克尔说，好啊，你为什么不把账单寄到宾夕法尼亚州斯克兰顿市，我不在乎巷23号呢？

1335
00:57:44.440 --> 00:57:46.000
I mean, what is happening?
我是说，这到底是怎么回事？

1336
00:57:46.000 --> 00:57:48.080
He's going to get his ass kicked out.
他会被人踢出去的。

1337
00:57:49.700 --> 00:57:50.260
Yeah.
是啊。

1338
00:57:50.520 --> 00:57:52.000
I think the rosé's hitting us.
我觉得我们有点喝高了。

1339
00:57:52.500 --> 00:57:53.060
Maybe.
也许吧。

1340
00:57:53.380 --> 00:57:53.580
Maybe.
也许吧。

1341
00:57:53.780 --> 00:57:56.980
I just want to do the whole rest of the episode as your journal, frankly.
说实话，我真想用你的日记风格把剩下的剧集讲完。

1342
00:57:58.780 --> 00:58:01.080
It delights me so much.
这让我太开心了。

1343
00:58:01.740 --> 00:58:02.800
Guest star alert.
客串明星预警。

1344
00:58:03.260 --> 00:58:06.000
Our manager Donna was played by Amy Peets.
我们的经理唐娜是由艾米·皮茨饰演的。

1345
00:58:06.520 --> 00:58:15.500
She was on the NBC sitcom Caroline in the City, for which she was nominated for a Screen Actors Guild Award for outstanding performance by a female actor in a comedy series.
她曾出演NBC情景喜剧《城市故事》，并凭借该剧获得了美国演员工会奖喜剧类剧集最佳女演员提名。

1346
00:58:16.000 --> 00:58:22.760
She's also had recurring roles on Modern Family, Animal Kingdom, and she appears in five episodes of The Office.
她还在《摩登家庭》和《野兽家族》中担任常驻角色，并出演了五集《办公室》。

1347
00:58:23.420 --> 00:58:29.260
She was also in a really good episode of Law & Order SVU, which I just watched the other day.
她还出演过一集非常精彩的《法律与秩序：特殊受害者》，我前几天刚看过。

1348
00:58:29.600 --> 00:58:30.340
Which one?
哪一集？

1349
00:58:30.340 --> 00:58:32.160
It's the one where she plays Mama Zoe.
就是她饰演佐伊妈妈的那一集。

1350
00:58:32.680 --> 00:58:33.860
She's really good in it.
她在里面演得真好。

1351
00:58:34.000 --> 00:58:34.920
It's a good episode.
这一集很棒。

1352
00:58:35.480 --> 00:58:41.740
During this scene, Pam and Jim are kind of trying to get Michael to calm down, and Pam wants to continue the pool game.
在这一幕里，帕姆和吉姆试图让迈克尔冷静下来，而帕姆想继续打台球。

1353
00:58:42.400 --> 00:58:44.320
I have another improv brag.
我还有个即兴表演的吹嘘点。

1354
00:58:44.720 --> 00:58:45.380
Do it.
说来听听。

1355
00:58:45.580 --> 00:58:48.760
I improvised the line, you guys are stripes, I think.
我即兴加了句台词：“我觉得你们是花色球”。

1356
00:58:48.760 --> 00:58:56.360
I think my scripted line was, I think she handled it pretty well, but instead I said, you guys are stripes, I think.
我想剧本原本的台词是“我觉得她处理得挺好”，但我改成了“我觉得你们是花色球”。

1357
00:58:56.540 --> 00:58:57.540
And you know why you said that?
你知道你为什么那么说吗？

1358
00:58:57.700 --> 00:58:58.520
Because I know about pool.
因为我懂台球。

1359
00:58:58.520 --> 00:58:59.380
Because you're a pool shark.
因为你是台球高手。

1360
00:58:59.520 --> 00:59:02.620
Yeah, I am, and I know that one person is stripes and one is solid.
没错，我是，而且我知道一个人打花色，一个人打全色。

1361
00:59:02.780 --> 00:59:03.000
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1362
00:59:03.280 --> 00:59:03.900
I know that.
我懂这个。

1363
00:59:04.040 --> 00:59:05.280
Sounds like one of my journal entries.
听起来像我写的日记。

1364
00:59:05.680 --> 00:59:06.840
You know what I want to find?
你知道我想找什么吗？

1365
00:59:07.040 --> 00:59:07.220
What?
什么？

1366
00:59:07.220 --> 00:59:11.980
I've got to have a journal entry about my plans to become a pool shark hustler.
我肯定有一篇日记是关于我计划成为台球骗子的。

1367
00:59:12.240 --> 00:59:12.700
Please.
拜托。

1368
00:59:12.820 --> 00:59:14.020
I must have one somewhere.
我肯定在哪儿写过。

1369
00:59:14.280 --> 00:59:14.330
Please.
拜托。

1370
00:59:14.440 --> 00:59:15.520
Surely I journaled that.
我肯定记过这个。

1371
00:59:15.840 --> 00:59:16.180
Surely.
肯定记过。

1372
00:59:17.460 --> 00:59:21.000
Michael is going to approach the manager and demand an apology.
迈克尔打算去找经理要求道歉。

1373
00:59:21.780 --> 00:59:23.420
I loved their back and forth.
我很喜欢他们之间的你来我往。

1374
00:59:23.660 --> 00:59:29.060
I loved it when he said the way he likes to be a manager has a dash of razzle-dazzle.
我特别喜欢他说自己当经理的风格带有一点“炫目色彩”。

1375
00:59:29.360 --> 00:59:29.640
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1376
00:59:29.640 --> 00:59:33.320
I was so curious if that was scripted or if Steve, like, threw that out there.
我很好奇那是剧本写的，还是史蒂夫随口发挥的。

1377
00:59:33.320 --> 00:59:34.480
I went to the shooting draft.
我查了拍摄用的剧本草稿。

1378
00:59:34.680 --> 00:59:35.440
It's in the script.
那是剧本里的。

1379
00:59:35.440 --> 00:59:37.660
A dash of razzle-dazzle.
带有一点“炫目色彩”。

1380
00:59:37.880 --> 00:59:38.940
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1381
00:59:39.380 --> 00:59:46.380
Donna clearly has the thing that Jan had, which is that she's attracted to tragedy because
唐娜显然有简的那种特质，就是她会被悲剧吸引，因为

1382
00:59:46.380 --> 00:59:50.820
she is sort of immediately smitten by Michael.
她对迈克尔有一种一见钟情的感觉。

1383
00:59:51.080 --> 00:59:53.700
Just like, what is this thing in front of me?
就像是，眼前这个东西到底是什么？

1384
00:59:53.960 --> 00:59:54.300
Yeah.
没错。

1385
00:59:54.620 --> 00:59:59.080
It's like the first time you see a kitten or something or a puppy, you're like, what is
就像你第一次看到小猫或小狗，你会想，这是

1386
00:59:59.080 --> 01:00:00.540
this creature?
什么生物？

1387
01:00:01.580 --> 01:00:03.480
I'm sort of drawn to it.
我被它吸引了。

1388
01:00:04.120 --> 01:00:05.580
But they have a repartee.
但他们之间确实有那种机智的对话。

1389
01:00:05.900 --> 01:00:06.400
They do.
确实有。

1390
01:00:07.140 --> 01:00:10.840
In their repartee, we find out that Michael has written a whole book in his head.
在他们的对话中，我们发现迈克尔在脑子里写了一整本书。

1391
01:00:11.000 --> 01:00:12.720
It's called Somehow I Manage.
书名叫《我如何管理》。

1392
01:00:12.980 --> 01:00:16.420
The book cover is him with his sleeves rolled up, shrugging.
封面是他卷起袖子，耸着肩的样子。

1393
01:00:17.840 --> 01:00:21.740
The manager says, have you read Lee Iacocca's classic book?
经理问：“你读过李·艾柯卡的经典著作吗？”

1394
01:00:21.920 --> 01:00:23.740
And Michael says, read it.
迈克尔回答：“读过。”

1395
01:00:23.860 --> 01:00:24.620
I own it.
我有这本书。

1396
01:00:24.760 --> 01:00:25.900
He hasn't read it.
他根本没读过。

1397
01:00:25.920 --> 01:00:27.260
But no, I haven't read it.
但其实，我没读过。

1398
01:00:27.940 --> 01:00:30.160
We had a fan question from Letty P.
我们收到了来自加州长滩的莱蒂·P的一位粉丝提问。

1399
01:00:30.380 --> 01:00:31.400
in Long Beach, California.
这是《办公室》里第二次提到李·艾柯卡的传记了。

1400
01:00:31.980 --> 01:00:35.640
This is the second time Lee Iacocca's biography is mentioned on The Office.
这是《办公室》里第二次提到李·艾柯卡的传记了。

1401
01:00:35.980 --> 01:00:40.660
I've watched this show so many times, and it's made me curious to actually pick up the book,
这部剧我看了很多遍，它让我对原著产生了兴趣，想去读一读，

1402
01:00:40.760 --> 01:00:41.720
and it's so good.
而且书真的很好看。

1403
01:00:41.720 --> 01:00:45.860
But why is it referred to so much when Michael hasn't even read it?
但为什么迈克尔连书都没读过，却总是提到它呢？

1404
01:00:46.540 --> 01:00:47.860
Well, Letty, I'll tell you.
嗯，莱蒂，我来告诉你。

1405
01:00:48.080 --> 01:00:49.280
It's because B.J.
因为B.J.

1406
01:00:49.400 --> 01:00:51.360
Novak's dad co-authored that book.
诺瓦克的父亲是那本书的合著者。

1407
01:00:51.540 --> 01:00:53.260
So this was a nod from B.J.
所以这是B.J.

1408
01:00:53.480 --> 01:00:54.000
to his dad.
向他父亲致敬。

1409
01:00:54.160 --> 01:00:55.080
This was a B.J.
这是B.J.

1410
01:00:55.260 --> 01:00:56.620
Easter egg for his dad.
给他父亲留下的彩蛋。

1411
01:00:57.100 --> 01:00:57.940
So cute.
太可爱了。

1412
01:00:58.380 --> 01:01:03.300
We really did that a lot on the show, like naming Pam and Jim's baby Cece and Sid and
我们在剧中确实经常这样做，比如给帕姆和吉姆的孩子取名西西，还有西德和

1413
01:01:03.300 --> 01:01:05.080
Dexter's and throwing the book in.
德克斯特，以及把那本书加进去。

1414
01:01:05.260 --> 01:01:06.680
We like to do that sort of thing.
我们很喜欢搞这种小动作。

1415
01:01:07.440 --> 01:01:12.200
Andy and Erin are still trying to hide their relationship because Andy does not want the
安迪和艾琳还在试图隐瞒他们的关系，因为安迪不想惹

1416
01:01:12.200 --> 01:01:12.520
drama.
麻烦。

1417
01:01:12.740 --> 01:01:13.440
He doesn't.
他确实不想。

1418
01:01:13.540 --> 01:01:14.420
Don't want the drama.
不想惹麻烦。

1419
01:01:15.300 --> 01:01:16.620
So he's like, you know what?
所以他心想，你知道吗？

1420
01:01:17.000 --> 01:01:21.100
Let's throw everyone off because a few people have made little comments that he thinks is
我们来混淆视听吧，因为有几个人说了些小评论，他觉得是

1421
01:01:21.100 --> 01:01:22.360
about him and Erin.
针对他和艾琳的。

1422
01:01:23.040 --> 01:01:24.760
He's like, I'm going to go talk to that girl.
他心想，我要去和那个女孩搭话。

1423
01:01:24.920 --> 01:01:26.100
You go talk to that guy.
你去和那个男人搭话。

1424
01:01:26.620 --> 01:01:28.240
Erin is going to sit next to a man.
艾琳要坐在一个男人旁边。

1425
01:01:28.420 --> 01:01:33.980
She's going to rub her hand on his thigh and say, hey, big boy, do you like it when
她要伸手摸他的大腿，然后说，嘿，大块头，你喜欢我

1426
01:01:33.980 --> 01:01:34.640
I do that?
这样做吗？

1427
01:01:34.880 --> 01:01:38.840
And Andy spits out his drink and is like, what are you doing?
然后安迪把喝的东西喷了出来，心想，你在干什么？

1428
01:01:39.380 --> 01:01:44.900
Well, the guy that Erin is talking to was played by our very own locations manager, Kyle
嗯，和艾琳搭话的那个男人是由我们的外景经理凯尔·

1429
01:01:44.900 --> 01:01:45.480
Alexander.
亚历山大扮演的。

1430
01:01:46.020 --> 01:01:52.580
They shared in the commentary that Kyle just has such a friendly demeanor that he wouldn't
他们在评论音轨里分享说，凯尔的举止非常友善，所以他看起来

1431
01:01:52.580 --> 01:01:53.940
seem threatening in any way.
一点威胁性都没有。

1432
01:01:53.940 --> 01:01:58.040
And probably nice for Ellie because he was someone that we all worked with.
而且这对艾莉来说可能也很好，因为他是我们大家都共事过的人。

1433
01:01:58.560 --> 01:01:58.680
Totally.
确实。

1434
01:01:59.680 --> 01:02:02.800
Andy kind of pulls Erin aside, pulls her into this photo booth.
安迪把艾琳拉到一边，把她拉进了那个照相亭。

1435
01:02:03.020 --> 01:02:07.240
And while they're in there, the camera is going off.
当他们在里面的时候，相机一直在闪。

1436
01:02:07.440 --> 01:02:08.500
While they're arguing.
就在他们争吵的时候。

1437
01:02:08.820 --> 01:02:09.200
Yes.
没错。

1438
01:02:09.560 --> 01:02:15.580
Matt said that getting this photo strip right was really important to him.
马特说，拍好这组照片对他来说真的很重要。

1439
01:02:15.580 --> 01:02:21.920
On the first day of this shoot week, Ed and Ellie got together with Michael Gallenberg,
在拍摄周的第一天，艾德和艾莉与我们的美术指导迈克尔·加伦伯格聚在一起，

1440
01:02:22.180 --> 01:02:27.900
our production designer, and he took photos of them, which Matt went over and he created
他为他们拍了照片，马特随后亲自挑选并制作了

1441
01:02:27.900 --> 01:02:30.760
the photo strip that would be used in this scene.
这场戏中要用到的照片条。

1442
01:02:31.120 --> 01:02:31.260
Yeah.
是的。

1443
01:02:31.280 --> 01:02:35.320
He talked about this on the commentary, how important the story of the photo strip was
他在评论音轨里谈到了这个照片条背后的故事对他来说

1444
01:02:35.320 --> 01:02:35.720
to him.
有多重要。

1445
01:02:35.880 --> 01:02:37.600
Well, he also sent in an audio clip.
嗯，他还发来了一段音频剪辑。

1446
01:02:37.720 --> 01:02:38.420
Let's give it a listen.
我们来听听看。

1447
01:02:38.420 --> 01:02:46.880
I also spent a lot of time working on the photos from the photo booth of Andy and Erin.
我还花了很多时间处理安迪和艾琳在照相亭拍的照片。

1448
01:02:47.160 --> 01:02:50.860
They tell a very sad story about their relationship.
它们讲述了一个关于他们关系的非常悲伤的故事。

1449
01:02:50.860 --> 01:02:57.200
If you notice them, they each show a different stage of their relationship, ending with Erin
如果你仔细观察，每一张都展示了他们关系的不同阶段，最后以艾琳

1450
01:02:57.200 --> 01:02:59.340
sad and by herself.
伤心且独自一人告终。

1451
01:02:59.340 --> 01:03:05.480
You know, when Andy looks at these photos, he realizes this isn't the relationship that
你知道，当安迪看着这些照片时，他意识到这并不是他想要的

1452
01:03:05.480 --> 01:03:06.040
he wants.
那种关系。

1453
01:03:06.040 --> 01:03:11.940
And he goes to the microphone to announce to everyone that he and Erin are a dating.
于是他走到麦克风前，向大家宣布他和艾琳正在约会。

1454
01:03:12.180 --> 01:03:13.040
They are a couple.
他们是一对情侣。

1455
01:03:13.220 --> 01:03:15.640
And it's a nice ending to their story.
这对他们的故事来说是一个美好的结局。

1456
01:03:17.680 --> 01:03:23.280
Sometimes those little props, designing those just right, really are important.
有时候那些小道具，把它们设计得恰到好处，真的很重要。

1457
01:03:23.480 --> 01:03:26.720
And after Matt said that, I went and I paused on the strip.
马特说完那番话后，我回去暂停在了那张照片条上。

1458
01:03:27.020 --> 01:03:27.260
Same.
我也是。

1459
01:03:27.520 --> 01:03:28.080
It's really good.
真的很棒。

1460
01:03:28.080 --> 01:03:29.120
It is really good.
确实很棒。

1461
01:03:29.200 --> 01:03:31.860
And it's something I missed the first time I watched it.
这是我第一次看的时候错过的细节。

1462
01:03:32.260 --> 01:03:34.760
And it's just one of those things in this rewatch.
这也是重温这部剧时发现的众多细节之一。

1463
01:03:34.960 --> 01:03:36.020
It's so fun to discover.
发现这些真的很有趣。

1464
01:03:36.460 --> 01:03:38.300
You know, I love a photo strip.
你知道，我超爱这种照片条。

1465
01:03:38.560 --> 01:03:42.060
I will go into any mall, kiosk, photo booth.
任何商场、小摊位、照相亭我都会去拍。

1466
01:03:42.280 --> 01:03:44.580
Lady, it's the cover of our book.
大姐，那可是我们书的封面啊。

1467
01:03:44.780 --> 01:03:45.580
The cover of our book is a photo strip.
我们书的封面就是一张照片条。

1468
01:03:45.700 --> 01:03:50.340
That I saved for 18 years.
我保存了18年的那张。

1469
01:03:50.780 --> 01:03:51.060
Yeah.
是啊。

1470
01:03:51.480 --> 01:03:53.080
That you insisted that we do.
那是你坚持要我们拍的。

1471
01:03:53.320 --> 01:03:53.740
I know.
我知道。

1472
01:03:53.920 --> 01:03:55.900
I tried to do the cough at our age thing.
我试着用了那种“我们这把年纪”的咳嗽暗示法。

1473
01:03:56.000 --> 01:03:56.640
It didn't work.
没成功。

1474
01:03:56.640 --> 01:04:02.200
Like, you know, where you say, like, like, where you cough something that you kind of want people to hear.
就是那种，你知道的，你想让别人听到什么，就故意咳嗽一声。

1475
01:04:02.420 --> 01:04:02.840
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1476
01:04:03.020 --> 01:04:05.500
Like, you know what I mean?
就像，你明白我的意思吗？

1477
01:04:08.220 --> 01:04:08.780
I do.
我明白。

1478
01:04:09.440 --> 01:04:09.960
Okay.
好吧。

1479
01:04:10.360 --> 01:04:11.220
Where are we?
我们讲到哪了？

1480
01:04:12.540 --> 01:04:15.100
Oh, Matt has not shown up.
噢，马特还没出现。

1481
01:04:15.840 --> 01:04:18.140
Oscar's been sitting with the warehouse guys forever.
奥斯卡已经在仓库那边和工人们坐了半天了。

1482
01:04:18.760 --> 01:04:19.540
I know.
我知道。

1483
01:04:19.880 --> 01:04:26.660
And Daryl is like, listen, I know he's super cute, but the truth is he's kind of a dum-dum.
达里尔就说，听着，我知道他超级可爱，但说实话，他有点笨笨的。

1484
01:04:26.900 --> 01:04:27.420
And Oscar.
还有奥斯卡。

1485
01:04:27.780 --> 01:04:29.500
Yeah, he's like, you guys aren't a good match.
对，他就像是在说，你们俩不合适。

1486
01:04:29.800 --> 01:04:30.060
No.
没错。

1487
01:04:30.300 --> 01:04:31.140
Daryl's trying.
达里尔在努力。

1488
01:04:31.400 --> 01:04:33.340
He's trying to look out for Oscar in this moment.
他此刻是在试着为奥斯卡着想。

1489
01:04:33.340 --> 01:04:37.520
In college, I dated just this real dum-dum.
我在大学时，也约会过一个真的很笨的家伙。

1490
01:04:37.660 --> 01:04:38.300
Hello, Rosé.
你好啊，罗泽。

1491
01:04:38.340 --> 01:04:39.380
So good looking.
长得真帅。

1492
01:04:39.540 --> 01:04:40.460
Settle in, Rosé.
坐好，罗泽。

1493
01:04:40.620 --> 01:04:41.380
What do you got for me?
你有什么要跟我说的吗？

1494
01:04:41.680 --> 01:04:42.020
Nothing.
没什么。

1495
01:04:42.340 --> 01:04:44.220
Just that, like, it was so clear to me.
只是，当时对我来说太明显了。

1496
01:04:44.380 --> 01:04:45.900
He was just super hottie.
他就是个超级大帅哥。

1497
01:04:45.980 --> 01:04:46.320
Eye candy.
秀色可餐。

1498
01:04:46.760 --> 01:04:47.000
Mm.
嗯。

1499
01:04:47.780 --> 01:04:49.000
And I don't know.
我也不知道。

1500
01:04:49.080 --> 01:04:50.220
It didn't last long.
反正没持续多久。

1501
01:04:50.420 --> 01:04:51.120
Was it fun?
好玩吗？

1502
01:04:51.460 --> 01:04:52.340
Not really.
不怎么好玩。

1503
01:04:52.600 --> 01:04:52.940
Oh.
噢。

1504
01:04:53.140 --> 01:04:54.060
Well, that's a bummer.
好吧，真扫兴。

1505
01:04:54.200 --> 01:04:54.760
I know.
我知道。

1506
01:04:55.420 --> 01:04:57.860
But I loved looking at him.
但我很喜欢看着他。

1507
01:04:57.980 --> 01:04:59.100
It was so beautiful.
那画面太美了。

1508
01:05:01.420 --> 01:05:02.680
So I get it, Oscar.
所以我理解你，奥斯卡。

1509
01:05:02.680 --> 01:05:03.840
What's your journal entry?
你的日记写了什么？

1510
01:05:06.360 --> 01:05:08.520
I looked at this guy for a while today.
我今天盯着那个家伙看了一会儿。

1511
01:05:10.180 --> 01:05:11.740
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

1512
01:05:12.120 --> 01:05:17.460
Just as maybe Oscar is considering that they aren't a match, Matt walks in.
就在奥斯卡可能觉得他们不合适的时候，马特走了进来。

1513
01:05:18.460 --> 01:05:19.340
Oscar's delighted.
奥斯卡很高兴。

1514
01:05:19.620 --> 01:05:20.540
He walks in.
他走了进来。

1515
01:05:20.680 --> 01:05:22.040
He wants to go play basketball.
他想去打篮球。

1516
01:05:22.240 --> 01:05:23.060
Oscar's like, yeah.
奥斯卡说，好啊。

1517
01:05:23.560 --> 01:05:26.300
The two of them shooting next to each other was so funny.
他们俩并排投篮的样子太搞笑了。

1518
01:05:26.460 --> 01:05:30.960
It was actually a note in the shooting draft that Oscar tries to shoot, and it, like,
剧本里确实有这么个备注，说奥斯卡尝试投篮，然后它，就像是，

1519
01:05:31.100 --> 01:05:35.260
ricochets off the, like, backboard, and, like, he's chasing it on the ground.
从篮板上弹开了，然后，他就在地上追着球跑。

1520
01:05:35.840 --> 01:05:41.280
I want to say it is very hard to be bad at things like that when you have to as an actor.
我想说的是，作为演员，要刻意表现得不擅长某事其实非常难。

1521
01:05:41.580 --> 01:05:46.120
Like, that was some really good bad basketball acting on Oscar's part.
比如，奥斯卡那段“不擅长打篮球”的演技真的很棒。

1522
01:05:46.260 --> 01:05:48.260
Yeah, he actually can, like, shoot pretty well.
是啊，他其实投篮投得挺好的。

1523
01:05:48.360 --> 01:05:48.560
Right.
没错。

1524
01:05:48.660 --> 01:05:52.360
I remember that from the basketball episode when all those guys started shooting.
我记得篮球那一集，当时所有人都开始投篮了。

1525
01:05:52.600 --> 01:05:52.780
Yeah.
是啊。

1526
01:05:53.060 --> 01:05:55.220
Well, we're going to wrap up a couple of storylines here.
好了，我们要在这里收尾几条故事线了。

1527
01:05:55.360 --> 01:05:56.560
We're getting near the end of the episode.
这一集快要结束了。

1528
01:05:56.960 --> 01:06:01.740
Andy's going to get on a loudspeaker, announces that he's been on a few successful dates with Aaron.
安迪要用扩音器宣布他和亚伦约会了几次，而且很成功。

1529
01:06:01.880 --> 01:06:02.860
There'll probably be more.
以后可能还会有更多次。

1530
01:06:03.080 --> 01:06:03.940
No one cares.
根本没人关心。

1531
01:06:04.480 --> 01:06:04.600
No.
没。

1532
01:06:04.600 --> 01:06:05.600
No one even looks over.
甚至没人抬头看一眼。

1533
01:06:06.400 --> 01:06:06.760
No.
没。

1534
01:06:07.720 --> 01:06:09.560
Andy and Aaron are so happy, though.
不过安迪和亚伦倒是很高兴。

1535
01:06:09.980 --> 01:06:10.620
Aaron especially.
尤其是亚伦。

1536
01:06:11.440 --> 01:06:15.840
Dwight and Isabel are leaving together when Angela approaches them.
德怀特和伊莎贝尔正要一起离开，安吉拉走近了他们。

1537
01:06:15.940 --> 01:06:16.660
Still lurking.
还在潜伏。

1538
01:06:17.060 --> 01:06:18.440
I don't think she was lurking.
我觉得她没在潜伏。

1539
01:06:18.660 --> 01:06:21.720
This was, like, a, like, full frontal approach.
这明明是，那种，正面迎击。

1540
01:06:22.000 --> 01:06:26.780
I know, but lurking in the sense that everywhere these people turn, you're on top of them.
我知道，但“潜伏”的意思是，无论这些人转向哪里，你都阴魂不散地跟着。

1541
01:06:26.980 --> 01:06:28.100
You're all over them.
你简直无处不在。

1542
01:06:28.100 --> 01:06:28.920
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

1543
01:06:29.360 --> 01:06:30.140
Rightfully so.
理应如此。

1544
01:06:30.280 --> 01:06:31.820
He should not have broken that contract.
他不该违背那份合同的。

1545
01:06:32.140 --> 01:06:33.780
I like Angela in this moment.
这一刻我挺喜欢安吉拉的。

1546
01:06:33.880 --> 01:06:36.380
Well, she's going to serve him papers to appear in court.
嗯，她要给他送传票，让他出庭。

1547
01:06:36.500 --> 01:06:37.100
That's right.
没错。

1548
01:06:37.220 --> 01:06:38.260
For breach of contract.
因为违约。

1549
01:06:38.280 --> 01:06:38.760
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1550
01:06:39.440 --> 01:06:41.240
Isabel whacks her on the forehead.
伊莎贝尔朝她额头上猛拍了一下。

1551
01:06:41.760 --> 01:06:44.960
We had a fan question from Stacey C in Charlotte, North Carolina.
我们收到了一位来自北卡罗来纳州夏洛特市的粉丝Stacey C的提问。

1552
01:06:45.300 --> 01:06:48.080
Angela, did she really smack you on the head?
安吉拉，她真的拍了你的头吗？

1553
01:06:48.340 --> 01:06:49.000
She did.
是的，她拍了。

1554
01:06:49.220 --> 01:06:49.940
That was real.
那是真的。

1555
01:06:50.420 --> 01:06:51.420
It was scripted.
那是剧本安排的。

1556
01:06:51.540 --> 01:06:52.360
It was scripted.
那是剧本安排的。

1557
01:06:52.740 --> 01:06:58.180
I want you to know that when this episode aired, people took to the message boards sympathizing for Angela.
我想让你知道，当这一集播出时，人们在留言板上纷纷表示同情安吉拉。

1558
01:06:58.360 --> 01:07:00.540
This never happened for my character.
我的角色从来没遇到过这种事。

1559
01:07:01.120 --> 01:07:02.860
I did not like that she hit you on the head.
我不喜欢她拍你头的那一幕。

1560
01:07:03.340 --> 01:07:04.320
I didn't like it.
我也不喜欢。

1561
01:07:04.400 --> 01:07:06.260
You didn't like it, and guess who else didn't like it?
你不喜欢，你猜还有谁也不喜欢？

1562
01:07:06.300 --> 01:07:06.520
Who?
谁？

1563
01:07:06.700 --> 01:07:07.460
Birdie Kinsey.
伯蒂·金西。

1564
01:07:07.760 --> 01:07:08.300
My mom.
我妈。

1565
01:07:08.640 --> 01:07:09.800
She did not care for it.
她很不高兴。

1566
01:07:09.960 --> 01:07:10.280
No.
没错。

1567
01:07:10.280 --> 01:07:12.520
Well, Angela is not going to be deterred.
好吧，安吉拉是不会被吓倒的。

1568
01:07:12.820 --> 01:07:15.660
She scurries off, but Dwight will be hearing from her in court.
她溜走了，但德怀特很快就会收到她的法院传票。

1569
01:07:16.140 --> 01:07:19.540
I mean, several people are brought together in this episode.
我是说，这一集里有几个人聚在了一起。

1570
01:07:19.720 --> 01:07:20.300
Andy, Aaron.
安迪，亚伦。

1571
01:07:20.720 --> 01:07:21.040
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1572
01:07:21.520 --> 01:07:22.380
Isabel and Dwight.
伊莎贝尔和德怀特。

1573
01:07:22.720 --> 01:07:23.260
And Michael.
还有迈克尔。

1574
01:07:24.120 --> 01:07:25.300
He's got a date.
他去约会了。

1575
01:07:25.700 --> 01:07:27.400
Date Mike actually came through.
“约会迈克”这次竟然真的成功了。

1576
01:07:27.740 --> 01:07:29.020
I mean, kind of.
我是说，算是吧。

1577
01:07:29.020 --> 01:07:30.580
He wasn't being Date Mike.
他当时并不是在扮演“约会迈克”。

1578
01:07:30.800 --> 01:07:35.720
He was just being, like, righteous Michael at the bar.
他只是在酒吧里表现得像个正义凛然的迈克。

1579
01:07:35.720 --> 01:07:37.640
Well, he thinks it worked once again.
嗯，他觉得这次又成功了。

1580
01:07:37.640 --> 01:07:42.360
But this episode ends with just an amazing tag.
但这一集的结尾有一个非常精彩的彩蛋。

1581
01:07:42.840 --> 01:07:43.640
Amazing.
太棒了。

1582
01:07:44.000 --> 01:07:45.840
It's one of my favorite of the whole series.
这是我整部剧里最喜欢的片段之一。

1583
01:07:46.080 --> 01:07:46.600
Agree.
同意。

1584
01:07:47.040 --> 01:07:51.620
It is Daryl and Hideo from The Warehouse.
那是达里尔和仓库里的秀夫。

1585
01:07:51.880 --> 01:07:57.540
And Daryl encourages Hideo to tell his story, his origin story.
达里尔鼓励秀夫讲出他的故事，他的身世故事。

1586
01:07:57.680 --> 01:07:57.840
Yeah.
没错。

1587
01:07:57.840 --> 01:08:00.380
Earlier in the episode, he sort of teases it to Oscar.
在这一集的前面，他曾向奥斯卡稍微透露过一点。

1588
01:08:00.540 --> 01:08:02.420
He's like, have you heard Hideo's story?
他说，你听过秀夫的故事吗？

1589
01:08:02.540 --> 01:08:03.480
I mean, it's fascinating.
我是说，那太迷人了。

1590
01:08:03.920 --> 01:08:04.000
Yeah.
是的。

1591
01:08:04.700 --> 01:08:05.420
And here it is.
现在故事来了。

1592
01:08:05.480 --> 01:08:06.260
He tells this story.
他讲了这个故事。

1593
01:08:06.600 --> 01:08:09.220
He says, in Japan, he was the top heart surgeon.
他说，在日本，他曾是顶尖的心脏外科医生。

1594
01:08:09.920 --> 01:08:15.920
But he made a mistake while operating on a Yakuza boss, who died as a result.
但他给一位黑帮老大做手术时出了差错，导致对方死亡。

1595
01:08:16.180 --> 01:08:21.540
So Hideo ran away to escape the wrath of the Yakuza, came to America on a fishing boat
所以秀夫为了躲避黑帮的报复逃跑了，坐着渔船来到美国，

1596
01:08:21.540 --> 01:08:22.980
with no food, no money.
没钱没食物。

1597
01:08:23.420 --> 01:08:24.660
Daryl gave him a job.
达里尔给了他一份工作。

1598
01:08:25.020 --> 01:08:28.760
Now he has an American car, a job, a woman.
现在他有了美国车，有了工作，还有了女人。

1599
01:08:29.340 --> 01:08:30.760
Daryl saved his life.
达里尔救了他的命。

1600
01:08:31.040 --> 01:08:32.300
But he has a secret.
但他有一个秘密。

1601
01:08:32.440 --> 01:08:32.820
TwiSt.
反转。

1602
01:08:33.280 --> 01:08:35.500
He killed the Yakuza boss on purpose.
他是故意杀了那个黑帮老大的。

1603
01:08:35.760 --> 01:08:37.240
He's a really good surgeon.
他是个非常出色的外科医生。

1604
01:08:37.440 --> 01:08:38.040
The beSt.
最棒的。

1605
01:08:38.840 --> 01:08:39.740
It's so good.
太棒了。

1606
01:08:39.900 --> 01:08:40.720
It's so good.
太棒了。

1607
01:08:40.900 --> 01:08:42.780
I slid into Hideo's DMs.
我给秀夫发了私信。

1608
01:08:42.920 --> 01:08:45.200
Hideo, if you hear this, check your DMs.
秀夫，如果你听到这个，记得看私信。

1609
01:08:45.300 --> 01:08:49.440
We would love to talk to you about your experience on The Office and this talking head.
我们很想和你聊聊你在《办公室》里的经历，以及这段采访。

1610
01:08:49.600 --> 01:08:50.820
You just crushed it.
你表现得太出色了。

1611
01:08:50.940 --> 01:08:52.160
We just think you're awesome.
我们觉得你太棒了。

1612
01:08:52.500 --> 01:08:56.320
Hideo had been on the show for a long time as one of the warehouse workers.
秀夫在剧里当了很久的仓库工人。

1613
01:08:57.660 --> 01:09:03.020
And BJ said in an interview that getting this tag into the show was a mission of his.
BJ在采访中说，把这个标签加入剧中是他的一个使命。

1614
01:09:03.020 --> 01:09:10.220
He said that he loved the idea that this character, who we've only seen in the background,
他说他很喜欢这个点子：这个我们平时只在背景里看到的角色，

1615
01:09:10.560 --> 01:09:18.580
had a life story infinitely more dramatic than anyone else the documentary crew had been following, but they never thought to ask.
竟然有着比纪录片摄制组跟拍的任何人都更戏剧性的人生故事，但他们却从未想过要问。

1616
01:09:18.580 --> 01:09:23.900
BJ also said that they shot six different versions of this in various places.
BJ还说，他们为这一幕在不同地点拍了六个版本。

1617
01:09:24.300 --> 01:09:28.680
They shot Hideo by himself in the warehouse, Hideo by himself in the bar.
他们拍了秀夫独自在仓库的镜头，还有秀夫独自在酒吧的镜头。

1618
01:09:29.020 --> 01:09:33.000
They shot Daryl and Hideo in the warehouse, Daryl and Hideo in the bar.
他们拍了达里尔和秀夫在仓库的镜头，还有达里尔和秀夫在酒吧的镜头。

1619
01:09:33.820 --> 01:09:37.420
And we also shot two totally different backstories.
而且我们还拍了两个完全不同的背景故事。

1620
01:09:38.020 --> 01:09:41.460
Well, I love that they chose the one with Daryl standing next to him.
嗯，我很高兴他们选择了达里尔站在他旁边的那个版本。

1621
01:09:41.580 --> 01:09:41.880
Me too.
我也是。

1622
01:09:41.880 --> 01:09:43.440
I thought it was really just perfect.
我觉得那简直太完美了。

1623
01:09:43.820 --> 01:09:47.540
I went to the candy bag in the shooting draft for this talking head.
我翻看了这段采访拍摄剧本里的备选方案。

1624
01:09:47.760 --> 01:09:48.660
And BJ is right.
BJ说得对。

1625
01:09:48.660 --> 01:09:49.580
There were many versions.
确实有很多版本。

1626
01:09:49.620 --> 01:09:51.680
I'm going to share with you two of my favorites.
我要和你们分享其中我最喜欢的两个。

1627
01:09:52.000 --> 01:09:52.200
Okay.
好的。

1628
01:09:52.560 --> 01:09:58.200
In one, Hideo's brother had put a hit out on him, and Hideo was traveling the world hiding.
其中一个版本里，秀夫的兄弟对他下了追杀令，秀夫为了躲避而周游世界。

1629
01:09:58.600 --> 01:10:00.240
That's the one that was in the shooting draft.
那个就是拍摄剧本里的版本。

1630
01:10:00.240 --> 01:10:02.740
I remember that one from the table read.
我记得剧本围读时有这个版本。

1631
01:10:02.740 --> 01:10:03.220
Yes.
是的。

1632
01:10:03.460 --> 01:10:09.700
In another one, Hideo was a sumo champion, and he traveled to India and then drank some
在另一个版本里，秀夫曾是相扑冠军，他去了印度，喝了某种

1633
01:10:09.700 --> 01:10:14.440
kind of tea there that made him not hungry and not want to eat, and he lost a bunch of
茶，导致他不再感到饥饿，也不想吃东西，结果他瘦了

1634
01:10:14.440 --> 01:10:18.160
weight, and his wife left him, and he was penniless, and he came to America.
一大圈，妻子也离开了他，他变得身无分文，最后来到了美国。

1635
01:10:18.680 --> 01:10:20.280
Well, I loved this one.
嗯，我喜欢这个版本。

1636
01:10:20.420 --> 01:10:26.340
I loved this one, and BJ shared on the commentary when Hideo says, American car, that Hideo improvised
我喜欢这个，而且BJ在评论音轨里分享过，当秀夫说“美国车”时，那是秀夫即兴

1637
01:10:26.340 --> 01:10:26.640
that.
发挥的。

1638
01:10:26.860 --> 01:10:27.320
Yes.
没错。

1639
01:10:27.780 --> 01:10:29.420
And BJ loved that.
BJ很喜欢那个。

1640
01:10:30.300 --> 01:10:32.060
Well, that was happy hour.
嗯，那是欢乐时光。

1641
01:10:34.180 --> 01:10:36.720
Guys, we're going to miss you while we're on our vacation.
伙计们，我们休假期间会想你们的。

1642
01:10:36.900 --> 01:10:38.020
We love you.
我们爱你们。

1643
01:10:38.160 --> 01:10:43.260
But like I said, we will be back July 15th for Secretary's Day with Miss Ellie Kemper.
但就像我说的，我们会在7月15日秘书节回归，届时会有艾莉·坎伯小姐做客。

1644
01:10:43.480 --> 01:10:47.100
We just want to say thank you to Matt Stone for his audio clips, and of course, Randy
我们想感谢马特·斯通提供的音频片段，当然还有兰迪·科德雷，

1645
01:10:47.100 --> 01:10:49.700
Cordray, who always gives us the behind-the-scenes details.
他总是为我们提供幕后细节。

1646
01:10:49.980 --> 01:10:54.960
And we hope this week you guys have a little bit of razzle-dazzle and a great week.
希望你们这周过得精彩纷呈，一切顺利。

1647
01:10:55.300 --> 01:10:55.900
Love ya.
爱你们。

1648
01:10:55.900 --> 01:10:56.740
Bye.
再见。

1649
